(68, '5a79b28a-43c3-4077-8048-8a32a0c9144c', 313, 'agent.turn.completed', 'computer', 'moonya', 'empty_recycle_bin', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"empty_recycle_bin-turn-1\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"The user wants me to empty the Windows Recycle Bin on this machine. I should use the shell executor to run the appropriate command to empty the recycle bin.\\n\\nThe standard way to empty the recycle bin via command line is:\\n- PowerShell: `Clear-RecycleBin -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue` (PowerShell 5.0+)\\n- Or `rd /s /q C:\\\\$Recycle.Bin` but that\'s not recommended\\n\\nLet me first check the recycle bin status, then empty it, then verify.\\n\\nI can use PowerShell:\\n1. Check current status: `Get-ChildItem -Path \'C:\\\\$Recycle.Bin\' -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Measure-Object` or use the Shell.Application COM object to count items.\\n2. Empty: `Clear-RecycleBin -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue`\\n3. Verify: check again that it\'s empty.\\n\\nLet me run these steps. First, let me check the current state of the recycle bin and then empty it.\\n\\nActually, let me do it step by step:\\n1. Check current state\\n2. Clear recycle bin\\n3. Verify empty\\n\\nLet me run the first command to check the state.\",\"content\":\"我来清空本机回收站。首先检查回收站当前状态：\",\"summary\":\"我来清空本机回收站。首先检查回收站当前状态：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":1,\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}}', '2026-08-03 08:08:22'),
