(437, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 1654, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"complete_and_run_app-turn-6\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Now I have a good picture. Let me understand the page functions signatures:\\n\\n- `WB.pages.home()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.work()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.todo()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.inbox()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.projects()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.projectDetail(id)` - takes id\\n- `WB.pages.log()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.meetings()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.study()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.tree()` - no args (line 121: `WB.navigate(\'#/study/tree\', p)` - passes params p, tree reads from WB.navigate params presumably)\\n- `WB.pages.knowledgeDetail(id)` - takes id\\n- `WB.pages.questions()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.wrong()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.plans()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.checkin()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.current()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.note()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.noteList()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.noteEdit(id)` - takes id\\n- `WB.pages.ideas()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.review()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.search()` - no args\\n- `WB.pages.settings()` - no args\\n\\nSo the routes:\\n- `#/home` → home\\n- `#/work` → work\\n- `#/work/todo` → todo\\n- `#/work/inbox` → inbox\\n- `#/work/projects` → projects\\n- `#/work/project/:id` → projectDetail(id)\\n- `#/work/log` → log\\n- `#/work/meetings` → meetings\\n- `#/study` → study\\n- `#/study/tree` → tree\\n- `#/study/knowledge/:id` → knowledgeDetail(id)\\n- `#/study/questions` → questions\\n- `#/study/wrong` → wrong\\n- `#/study/plans` → plans\\n- `#/study/checkin` → checkin\\n- `#/study/current` → current\\n- `#/note` → note\\n- `#/note/list` → noteList\\n- `#/note/new` → noteEdit(new)? Let me check how noteEdit handles \'new\' - need to look at pages-note.js around line 161.\\n- `#/note/edit/:id` → noteEdit(id)\\n- `#/note/ideas` → ideas\\n- `#/note/review` → review\\n- `#/search` → search\\n- `#/settings` → settings\\n\\nLet me check how the pages read params. Let me look at the beginning of pages-work.js and pages-study.js and pages-note.js to see how they get params (from WB.navigate storage). Also check pages-study.js tree function at line 69-121 and knowledgeDetail, questions with focus, noteEdit, etc.\\n\\nLet me read key portions of the pages files to understand param reading.\",\"content\":\"现在查看各页面如何读取参数（tree、questions 的 focus、noteEdit 的 new 等），先读 pages-study.js 和 pages-note.js 关键段：\",\"summary\":\"现在查看各页面如何读取参数（tree、questions 的 focus、noteEdit 的 new 等），先读 pages-study.js 和 pages-note.js 关键段：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":6,\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}}', '2026-08-03 10:10:55'),
