(456, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 1829, 'tool.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', 'call_01_oRFTS9pF98sItGV4ZWHs2534', '{\"tool_key\":\"grep\",\"ok\":true,\"content\":\"{\\\"success\\\":true,\\\"matches\\\":[],\\\"truncated\\\":false,\\\"truncated_files\\\":[]}\",\"error\":null,\"stage\":null,\"status\":null,\"error_code\":null,\"command_fingerprint\":null,\"operation_receipt\":null}', '2026-08-03 10:11:12'),
(457, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 1830, 'agent.turn.started', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"complete_and_run_app-turn-8\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":8}}', '2026-08-03 10:11:12'),
(458, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 2709, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"complete_and_run_app-turn-8\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Now the pattern is clear:\\n\\n**Param convention**: Pages read params via `this._xxx` (underscore-prefixed properties). So `WB.navigate(hash, params)` should call the page function with `this` bound to an object where each param key becomes `_key`. E.g., `WB.navigate(\'#/work/todo\', { filter: \'all\' })` → the todo page reads `this._filter`.\\n\\nParams keys used:\\n- `filter` (work/todo)\\n- `kw` (work/projects, study/tree, study/questions, note/list)\\n- `tab` (work/projectDetail, study/wrong, note/list? no — note list uses mood/tag/kw/select)\\n- `date` (work/log)\\n- `selected` (study/tree)\\n- `mod`, `tag`, `src`, `focus` (study/questions)\\n- `type` (study/plans)\\n- `month` (study/current, note/review)\\n- `mood`, `select` (note/list, ideas)\\n\\nSo in WB.navigate, we need to transform params `{ filter: x }` into `{ _filter: x }` and call `page.call(paramsWithUnderscore, idArg?)`.\\n\\nWait — but the pages like `tree` use `this._kw`, so when WB.navigate stores params and later the page fn is called, the caller must set `this` to `{ _kw: ... }`.\\n\\nAlso `#/study/questions?focus=\' + c.dataset.q` — line 244 of pages-study.js sets `location.hash = \'#/study/questions?focus=...\'`. So hash can include a query string! The hash parser should handle query string: split on `?` — path part before `?`, query params after. The focus param is read as `this._focus`.\\n\\nSo my hash parser needs to:\\n1. Strip leading `#`\\n2. Split off query string after `?` and parse into params\\n3. Split path segments\\n4. Match against route patterns with `:id` placeholders\\n\\nRoutes needed (from the code):\\n- `#/home` → home\\n- `#/work` → work\\n- `#/work/todo` → todo\\n- `#/work/inbox` → inbox\\n- `#/work/projects` → projects\\n- `#/work/project/:id` → projectDetail(id)\\n- `#/work/log` → log\\n- `#/work/meetings` → meetings\\n- `#/study` → study\\n- `#/study/tree` → tree\\n- `#/study/knowledge/:id` → knowledgeDetail(id)\\n- `#/study/questions` → questions\\n- `#/study/wrong` → wrong\\n- `#/study/plans` → plans\\n- `#/study/checkin` → checkin\\n- `#/study/current` → current\\n- `#/note` → note\\n- `#/note/list` → noteList\\n- `#/note/new` → noteEdit(\'new\')? Let me check noteEdit signature - line 161: `WB.pages.noteEdit = function (id) {`. Let me look at how noteEdit handles \'new\'.\\n- `#/note/edit/:id` → noteEdit(id)\\n- `#/note/ideas` → ideas\\n- `#/note/review` → review\\n- `#/search` → search\\n- `#/settings` → settings\\n\\nLet me look at noteEdit to see how \'new\' is handled. Also check projectDetail and knowledgeDetail signatures — they take `id` as first arg.\\n\\nLet me read pages-note.js noteEdit (line 161-318) and pages-work.js projectDetail (439-592) briefly to confirm signature, plus pages-work.js todo (167-252) for the filter param.\",\"content\":\"参数约定已明确：页面通过 `this._xxx` 读取 WB.navigate 传入的 params（需加下划线前缀）。还需确认 noteEdit 对 `new` 的处理和带参函数签名：\",\"summary\":\"参数约定已明确：页面通过 `this._xxx` 读取 WB.navigate 传入的 params（需加下划线前缀）。还需确认 noteEdit 对 `new` 的处理和带参函数签名：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":8,\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}}', '2026-08-03 10:11:24'),
