(468, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 4007, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"complete_and_run_app-turn-9\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Now the API surface is fully clear:\\n\\n**Page function signatures:**\\n- `WB.pages.home()` \\n- `WB.pages.work()`\\n- `WB.pages.todo()` — reads `this._filter`\\n- `WB.pages.inbox()`\\n- `WB.pages.projects()` — reads `this._kw`\\n- `WB.pages.projectDetail(id)` — reads `this._tab`, `id` from route\\n- `WB.pages.log()` — reads `this._date`\\n- `WB.pages.meetings()`\\n- `WB.pages.study()`\\n- `WB.pages.tree()` — reads `this._kw`, `this._selected`\\n- `WB.pages.knowledgeDetail(id)`\\n- `WB.pages.questions()` — reads `this._mod`, `this._tag`, `this._src`, `this._kw`, `this._focus`\\n- `WB.pages.wrong()` — reads `this._tab`\\n- `WB.pages.plans()` — reads `this._type`\\n- `WB.pages.checkin()`\\n- `WB.pages.current()` — reads `this._month`, `this._tag`\\n- `WB.pages.note()`\\n- `WB.pages.noteList()` — reads `this._mood`, `this._tag`, `this._kw`, `this._select`\\n- `WB.pages.noteEdit(id)` — `id === \'new\'` creates new\\n- `WB.pages.ideas()` — reads `this._select`\\n- `WB.pages.review()` — reads `this._month`\\n- `WB.pages.search()`\\n- `WB.pages.settings()`\\n\\n**Routes (hash):**\\n- `#/home` → home\\n- `#/work` → work\\n- `#/work/todo` → todo\\n- `#/work/inbox` → inbox\\n- `#/work/projects` → projects\\n- `#/work/project/:id` → projectDetail(id)\\n- `#/work/log` → log\\n- `#/work/meetings` → meetings\\n- `#/study` → study\\n- `#/study/tree` → tree\\n- `#/study/knowledge/:id` → knowledgeDetail(id)\\n- `#/study/questions` → questions (query `?focus=xxx` → `_focus`)\\n- `#/study/wrong` → wrong\\n- `#/study/plans` → plans\\n- `#/study/checkin` → checkin\\n- `#/study/current` → current\\n- `#/note` → note\\n- `#/note/list` → noteList\\n- `#/note/new` → noteEdit(\'new\')\\n- `#/note/edit/:id` → noteEdit(id)\\n- `#/note/ideas` → ideas\\n- `#/note/review` → review\\n- `#/search` → search\\n- `#/settings` → settings\\n\\n**Params**: pages read `this._xxx`. So in `WB.navigate(hashOrPath, params)`, we should:\\n1. Set `location.hash = hashOrPath` (normalizing)\\n2. Store params in a module-level `pendingParams` object\\n3. When rendering the page, call `pageFn.call(Object.assign({}, pendingParams with underscore prefixes), id)` — with `this` bound to params object with `_` prefixed keys.\\n\\nNote the \\\"暂存 params 供目标页面 bind 读取\\\" (stash params for target page\'s bind to read). Actually pages read `this._xxx` inside the render function itself (the outer function that returns {html, bind}). E.g. `WB.pages.todo = function () { const filter = this._filter || \'all\'; ...}`. So the `this` binding must be applied when calling the outer render function. The bind function returned is a closure that uses `content`, so it works.\\n\\nBut careful: `WB.pages.todo` is called with `this` bound to params. `this._filter` is read at render time. The `bind` closure doesn\'t use `this`. OK.\\n\\nHowever — in `pages-note.js` line 110: `const rerender = () => { const s = state(); WB.navigate(\'#/note/list\', { mood: s.mood, tag: s.tag, kw: s.kw, select: this._select ? \'1\' : \'\' }); };` — here `this` inside `bind` refers to the `this` of the outer function IF bind is a regular function... Actually `bind` is an arrow-less function? Let me check: in pages they write `const bind = () => {...}` — arrow function, so `this` is lexically bound to the outer function\'s `this` (the params object). Good — so if we call page with `.call(paramsObj)`, `this._select` inside bind arrow function still refers to paramsObj. \\n\\nFor `noteEdit`, the signature is `function (id)`. So we call `page.call(paramsObj, id)`. The `id` is the route param. For `#/note/new`, we pass id=\'new\'.\\n\\nNow the topbar title and search entries, sidebar, theme, font scale, persistence of collapsed state, etc.\\n\\nLet me check CSS classes to use: `.sidebar`, `.topbar`, `.glass`, `.page`, `.content`, `.main-wrap`. Let me look at style.css for sidebar/topbar structure to write matching markup. Let me grep the CSS for relevant classes: `.sidebar`, `.topbar`, `.side-`, `.topbar-`, `.sidebar-collapsed`, etc.\\n\\nAlso need to know: `--accent`, CSS variables, dark theme class name (`.dark`? `[data-theme=\\\"dark\\\"]`? `html.dark`?). Let me check style.css.\",\"content\":\"API 全部确认。现在查看 CSS 中 sidebar/topbar/主题相关类的具体结构，确保渲染的标记与样式衔接：\",\"summary\":\"API 全部确认。现在查看 CSS 中 sidebar/topbar/主题相关类的具体结构，确保渲染的标记与样式衔接：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":9,\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}}', '2026-08-03 10:11:45'),
(469, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 4008, 'tool.started', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', 'call_00_OSjrsmECBuwzz8Y4l8R96616', '{\"tool_key\":\"grep\",\"display_name\":\"Grep\",\"arguments\":{\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"path\":\"D:\\\\Project\\\\Project\\\\ccee\\\\web1\\\\css\\\\style.css\",\"pattern\":\"^\\\\s*\\\\.(sidebar|topbar|main-wrap|content|side-|top-|sb-|tb-)[^{]*\\\\{|^\\\\s*:root|^\\\\s*\\\\[data-theme|^\\\\s*html\\\\.|^\\\\s*\\\\.dark|^\\\\s*body\",\"show_line_numbers\":true},\"effect\":\"read\",\"risk_level\":\"low\",\"phase\":null,\"operation_id\":null,\"intent\":null,\"shell\":null,\"command_fingerprint\":null}', '2026-08-03 10:11:45'),
