(489, 'f411d4dc-43b0-4d3d-9b6d-b8c94efdab3b', 4983, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'complete_and_run_app', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"complete_and_run_app-turn-12\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Now I have the full picture:\\n\\n**Theme**: `.theme-light` / `.theme-dark` classes on `document.documentElement`. For \\\"system\\\" mode, need to follow `prefers-color-scheme`. Approach: `applyTheme()` sets `document.documentElement.className` — but careful: we shouldn\'t wipe other classes. We can manage via `data-theme` attribute or class toggling. Simplest: keep a module var `currentThemeClass`, and toggle `.theme-light`/`.theme-dark` classes on `document.documentElement`, and also set `color-scheme` property. For system: listen to `matchMedia(\'(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\')` changes and re-apply.\\n\\nAlso `fontScale`: settings.fontSize (13-18px) applied to `document.documentElement.style.fontSize`. Wait — CSS uses `font-size: 15px` on body, and rems? The settings page itself sets `document.documentElement.style.fontSize = st.fontSize + \'px\'`. The requirement says \\\"应用 fontScale\\\". The spec says apply fontScale. Since settings page already directly sets `document.documentElement.style.fontSize`, my applyTheme should do the same: set fontSize based on store settings. But if CSS is px-based, changing root font-size won\'t scale. Hmm — the body font-size is 15px fixed, not rem. So setting `document.documentElement.style.fontSize` alone won\'t change actual text size...\\n\\nBut the requirement in the task says: \\\"WB.applyTheme()：按 store 中 settings.theme（light/dark/system）切换 document.documentElement 主题类并应用 fontScale\\\". So applyTheme must apply fontScale too. Since the settings page already sets root font-size and presumably that\'s the intended mechanism, I\'ll keep it consistent: applyTheme sets `document.documentElement.style.fontSize = settings.fontSize + \'px\'`. To make it actually affect the UI, body font-size could be set in rem... but body is 15px fixed. \\n\\nHmm, should I also set body style? To be safe and consistent with the settings page behavior (which only sets root fontSize), I\'ll do the same in applyTheme. But for it to actually scale, I could also apply a scale factor via `zoom`? No — cleaner: set `document.documentElement.style.fontSize` AND set body font-size via CSS var? The CSS body font-size is fixed px.\\n\\nActually wait — maybe better approach: applyFontScale via a CSS variable? Let me check if CSS uses any rem units... Let me quickly grep for `rem` in style.css. If CSS uses rem widely, setting root font-size works. If it\'s all px, root font-size does nothing visible. Let me check.\\n\\nActually the cleanest robust approach that matches \\\"fontScale\\\" and \\\"即时生效\\\": set `document.documentElement.style.fontSize` (as settings page does) AND add a small inline style on body `font-size: calc(...)`? That would conflict with CSS `body { font-size: 15px }` — inline style wins. But then only body text scales, rem-based things scale too.\\n\\nHmm, but modifying body inline style from app.js is fine. Let me check rem usage first.\\n\\nAlso note: `#app { height: 100vh }` and content scrolls internally — `.content { flex:1; overflow-y:auto }`. Good, matches \\\"主内容区内部滚动\\\".\\n\\nLet me check rem usage and any existing `data-sidebar`/persistence conventions, plus `.page` class and `page-head`.\",\"content\":\"主题机制确认：`.theme-light`/`.theme-dark` 加在 documentElement 上。检查 CSS 中 rem 的使用情况（决定 fontScale 实现方式）以及 .page 相关类：\",\"summary\":\"主题机制确认：`.theme-light`/`.theme-dark` 加在 documentElement 上。检查 CSS 中 rem 的使用情况（决定 fontScale 实现方式）以及 .page 相关类：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":12,\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}}', '2026-08-03 10:12:34'),
