(619, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 674, 'agent.turn.completed', 'file', 'moonya', 'read_design_prompt', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"read_design_prompt-turn-1\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"The user wants me to read a file at D:\\\\Project\\\\Project\\\\ccee\\\\web1\\\\工作台设计提示词.md and return the full original content without summarizing or rewriting.\\n\\nLet me use the read_file tool. However, there\'s a concern: the file might be large (10MB limit). Let me first check the file exists and its size, then read it. I can use read_file directly, but if it\'s too large, I may need to read in segments.\\n\\nLet me start by checking the file and reading it. I could use list_files or just try read_file directly. Let me try read_file first - if it fails or is truncated, I\'ll adjust.\\n\\nActually, to be safe, let me first check the directory and file size using shell or list_files, then read in chunks. But read_file has a default 10MB limit. Let me just try read_file with a large limit.\\n\\nLet me do a quick inspect first to know the file size. I\'ll use shell_executor with phase=inspect to check file existence and size, and simultaneously try reading the file. Actually, I should do dependent operations - read_file is the main thing. Let me first check size to decide chunking strategy.\\n\\nI can do both in parallel: list_files on the directory and a shell inspect to get file size. Then read the file.\",\"content\":\"我先确认文件是否存在及其大小，以便完整读取。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"我先确认文件是否存在及其大小，以便完整读取。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":1,\"round\":1,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":1,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:03:03'),
