(854, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 77431, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'skeleton', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"skeleton-turn-11\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"All files created. Now verify:\\n\\n1. node --check each JS file (act phase since node invocation was classified unknown... wait, node --check is read-only but the preflight classified node -v as unknown. Let me try PowerShell with `& node --check` — hmm, the earlier attempt with cmd `node -v` was classified unknown and rejected in inspect phase. Maybe in verify phase it will be allowed since verify allows read-only queries... The rule: \\\"inspect 阶段只允许已证明为只读的命令\\\". node --check is read-only in effect. The classifier said \\\"unknown\\\". Let me try running it in act phase? Actually running node --check is a verification, not a change. But preflight might reject in verify too if classified unknown.\\n\\nAlternative: use PowerShell\'s built-in? No JS parser. Hmm.\\n\\nLet me try `node --check` with shell=cmd in phase=verify — the preflight may allow it if it proves read-only... It classified \\\"node -v\\\" as unknown risk=high earlier. Maybe with the file path as argument it can be proven? Unlikely.\\n\\nAlternative approach: use PowerShell to check file existence and structure (Get-ChildItem, Get-Content). For syntax check, I could try using node via a wrapper that the classifier can\'t prove... Let me just try node --check in verify phase and see.\\n\\nActually, another idea: Python-based JS syntax check? Python has no JS parser. But I can do a bracket-balance/paren check for sanity.\\n\\nLet me first try node --check in verify phase. If rejected, fall back to Python-based structural checks + careful manual review.\",\"content\":\"所有文件已创建。现在进行验证——先用 `node --check` 对每个 JS 文件做语法校验：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"所有文件已创建。现在进行验证——先用 `node --check` 对每个 JS 文件做语法校验：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":11,\"round\":11,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":11,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:21:26'),
(855, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 77432, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_work', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_work-turn-11\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"意外！work.js 文件只有 1588 字符，内容是某个完全不同的文件（有 `App.navigate(nav.dataset.nav)` 等）——这看起来像是另一个 agent（并行任务）刚刚创建/覆盖了 work.js！文件末尾是 `})();`，说明它是个完整的文件。长度 1588 意味着它不是我的内容（我的内容有数万字符）。\\n\\n可能另一个并行任务（pages_work 之外的其他 agent）也在创建 js/pages/work.js？或者我的 create_file 被覆盖了。让我读取当前文件内容看看是什么。\",\"content\":\"work.js 已被其他并行任务覆盖（内容与我写入的不同）。先读取当前内容确认情况：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"work.js 已被其他并行任务覆盖（内容与我写入的不同）。先读取当前内容确认情况：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":11,\"round\":11,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":11,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:21:26');
INSERT INTO `team_run_events` (`id`, `run_id`, `seq`, `event_name`, `agent_key`, `parent_agent_key`, `task_id`, `tool_call_id`, `payload`, `created_at`) VALUES
(856, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 77433, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-11\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Now I understand the full contract:\\n\\n**Router**: \\n- `routes[path] = definition` — exact match only. No dynamic segment matching! `\'/study/knowledge/:id\'` won\'t match a hash of `#/study/knowledge/abc` — that would fall to the 404 page.\\n- BUT: `render(path)` and `mount(el, path)` receive `path` — the actual path from the hash.\\n- Since there\'s no dynamic matching, how do I handle `/study/knowledge/:id`? The task says \\\"动态路径需处理 id\\\". \\n\\nHmm. The task states: 通过 window.App.registerPage(path, ...) 注册，必须实现的页面及要求：3. \'/study/knowledge/:id\' 知识点详情（动态路径需处理 id）.\\n\\nThe router only does exact matching. Options:\\n1. Register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' as a literal path — the router will treat it as an exact string. But then navigating to \'#/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\' won\'t match.\\n2. Since the task says \\\"若发现契约缺失先按现有契约完成，不要改动骨架文件\\\" — the contract (router) doesn\'t support dynamic paths. I must not modify skeleton files (router.js is a skeleton file — \\\"不要改动骨架文件\\\"). So I need to work within the contract.\\n\\nApproach: Register the static path \'/study/knowledge\' for the tree page. For detail pages, I can register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' — but since the router doesn\'t support it... hmm.\\n\\nWait — maybe the intended pattern is: the detail page is navigated with a hash like \'#/study/knowledge/xxx\' where xxx is the id, and the page module handles it. But the router will 404 on that.\\n\\nAlternative: I can register multiple exact paths? No — ids are dynamic.\\n\\nBest approach given constraints: Register a literal route \'/study/knowledge/:id\' AND handle the actual dynamic navigation by using hash paths that DO match. Actually, since I can\'t modify the router, the cleanest robust solution:\\n\\n- In `render(path)` and `mount(el, path)`, `path` is the full hash-derived path. So when user navigates to \'#/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\', router looks up routes[\'/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\'] — not found → fallback 404.\\n\\nSo I MUST register the exact paths I navigate to. For dynamic ids, that\'s impossible in general.\\n\\nSolution: register both:\\n1. \'/study/knowledge\' — tree page.\\n2. \'/study/knowledge/:id\' — literal registration per the task requirement. This registers the literal string path \':id\'. This satisfies \\\"通过 registerPage 注册 \'/study/knowledge/:id\'\\\" literally, but navigation to actual ids won\'t work via hash alone.\\n\\nHmm, but the acceptance criteria says: \\\"浏览器直接打开 index.html 后可通过侧边栏或直接改 hash 进入上述每个页面\\\". For knowledge detail, \\\"直接改 hash 进入\\\" would be \'#/study/knowledge/<id>\'.\\n\\nWait, let me re-read the router code... `routes[path]` exact lookup. No wildcard except \'*\'.\\n\\nHmm, is there a possibility the other agents\' task includes extending router for dynamic routes? The task said \\\"不要改动骨架文件\\\" for me. The router.js is a skeleton file (js/router.js). I shouldn\'t modify it.\\n\\nPractical robust approach that satisfies both requirements without touching the router:\\n- Register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' as the literal route (per task requirement).\\n- ALSO handle dynamic ids by parsing the hash in the \'/study/knowledge\' tree page? No...\\n\\nAlternative approach: Since unmount/render lifecycle is per exact path, and we can\'t know ids in advance... \\n\\nActually wait — think again. I can register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' literally. Then when I navigate from the tree, I use `App.navigate(\'/study/knowledge/:id\')`? That\'s silly.\\n\\nBetter: I can register the literal pattern AND, at script load, also dynamically register specific known seed ids? No — ids are dynamic (user can add knowledge points? Actually knowledge points aren\'t user-created in the spec — only mastery updates. The seed ids are fixed: seed-know-1..4. But new knowledge could be added via import).\\n\\nHmm, what about intercepting at the router level via a hook? No, router doesn\'t support prefix matching.\\n\\nOK here\'s another thought: the requirement list says \\\"动态路径需处理 id\\\" — the expected design is that my page module handles parsing of the id from the path. Given the skeleton router lacks dynamic matching, a defensible implementation that still meets the acceptance criteria:\\n\\n1. Register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' with the detail page definition — matches the required contract exactly (literal registration).\\n2. Additionally, make the detail page reachable via hash by registering a catch for the actual dynamic paths? Impossible without modifying router.\\n\\nAlternative pragmatic approach: use the router\'s fallback? No — \'*\' is 404.\\n\\nHmm wait, actually, maybe I should reconsider: is router.js something \\\"another agent\\\" will extend later to support dynamic segments? The task says the contract is \\\"以 js/app.js 顶部注释及 App.store API 为准\\\" and \\\"若发现契约缺失先按现有契约完成\\\". The app.js comment says: \\\"path：形如 \'/home\'、\'/work\'、\'/work/todos\'；\'*\' 表示 404 兜底页。\\\" — no dynamic path support mentioned. So the contract as-is doesn\'t support \':id\' dynamic matching. \\\"若发现契约缺失先按现有契约完成\\\" means: if the contract is missing something, complete the work per the existing contract — i.e., work within it.\\n\\nSo my approach:\\n- Register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' literally (satisfies the \\\"registered\\\" requirement; the router treats \':id\' as literal text).\\n- For actual navigation with dynamic ids, I\'ll register the detail page under BOTH the literal \'/study/knowledge/:id\' AND handle real hash paths by... hmm.\\n\\nHold on. Let me think about what actually needs to work for acceptance:\\n1. Sidebar navigation to each page — fixed paths work.\\n2. Direct hash entry to each page — fixed paths work.\\n3. Core interactions: knowledge tree → click card → detail page. This navigation must work. If I navigate to \'#/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\', the router 404s unless that exact path is registered.\\n\\nSince ids come from seed data (fixed set) and user-created content, I can\'t pre-register all.\\n\\nBest solution within constraints: **Make the detail page work under any hash that starts with \'/study/knowledge/\'** — impossible with exact-match router.\\n\\nAlternative: Navigate to detail using a FIXED path with query-ish segment the router can match? Router matches exact strings only, and parsePath just strips \'#\'. So \'#/study/knowledge/detail/seed-know-1\' → path \'/study/knowledge/detail/seed-know-1\' — still dynamic.\\n\\nHmm what about: \'#/study/knowledge?id=xxx\' → path would be \'/study/knowledge?id=xxx\' — no exact match either.\\n\\nOK so the only way for dynamic ids to work is if the router supports prefix matching. It doesn\'t. Options:\\na) Modify router.js to add prefix matching — violates \\\"不要改动骨架文件\\\".\\nb) Register each id\'s path dynamically — works for seed + created points, since knowledge points are NOT user-creatable in the spec (only questions, plans, shizheng, checkins are; knowledge tree is fixed hierarchy with mastery updates). Actually knowledge points... The spec for knowledge tree: \\\"右侧为选中模块的知识点卡片列表\\\" — points exist per module with mastery etc. No UI for adding knowledge points. So knowledge ids are effectively the seed ones (and any from import). Seed ids: seed-know-1..4. But their path field is like \'行测 > 言语理解 > 逻辑填空\'.\\n\\nc) Use the literal \'/study/knowledge/:id\' route and parse the id from path — i.e., when navigating from the tree, use App.navigate(\'/study/knowledge/\' + id) which produces \'#/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\'... 404. No good.\\n\\nd) **Register a generic route for detail via the fallback of exact registration at runtime**: Since I can\'t modify the router, but I CAN register additional exact routes at runtime! When the user opens a knowledge detail, I could register the exact path for that id on the fly before navigating:\\n\\n```js\\nfunction openKnowledge(id) {\\n  if (!window.WorkbenchRouter) return;\\n  // ensure route for this id\\n  window.WorkbenchRouter.register(\'/study/knowledge/\' + id, KNOWLEDGE_DETAIL_DEF);\\n  App.navigate(\'/study/knowledge/\' + id);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis registers the exact dynamic path with the same definition. It works for navigation from within the app. But \\\"直接改 hash 进入\\\" (\'#/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\' typed in address bar) would 404 unless the route was registered during a previous session... routes are per-page-load. On fresh load with \'#/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\', router.render() looks up routes — not registered → fallback 404.\\n\\nHmm. But wait — page scripts run before boot? Load order: store.js, router.js, app.js, pages/*.js, then app.js boot happens on DOMContentLoaded. Pages/*.js scripts — if they\'re loaded synchronously before DOMContentLoaded, they run before boot and can register routes. So at script load time, I can pre-register routes for ALL seed knowledge ids (they\'re deterministic from store seed data? Actually store data can be user-modified and persisted — ids unknown in general).\\n\\nPragmatic robust approach: At script load, register the detail definition under the literal \'/study/knowledge/:id\' (contract compliance), AND ALSO dynamically register every existing knowledge id found in App.store.knowledge.list() — covering seed data and any persisted data (after refresh, store loads persisted data, so all existing knowledge ids get registered). For NEW knowledge added via import, we\'d need to re-register — but knowledge isn\'t addable via UI in this module. For safety, when opening detail from tree, re-register the exact path before navigating (covers any id not pre-registered).\\n\\nAdditionally, to handle \\\"直接改 hash 进入\\\" for an id not yet registered: I could also hook into... hmm, can\'t hook router. But actually — wait. I could make the detail page reachable under a fixed path with the id as a query param that the router WILL match? No, router matches exact.\\n\\nHmm, alternatively I could register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' AND make the tree page at \'/study/knowledge\' handle a hash like \'#/study/knowledge/<id>\'... no.\\n\\nActually — hmm, wait. What about registering the detail page for ANY hash by using a fixed set of common patterns? No.\\n\\nLet me reconsider: maybe the intended solution across agents is that router.js will be extended by another agent to support \':id\' patterns. The task explicitly says \\\"动态路径需处理 id\\\" and \\\"若发现契约缺失先按现有契约完成，不要改动骨架文件\\\". \\\"先按现有契约完成\\\" — complete per existing contract. So register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' literally (that\'s what the contract allows), parse the id from the path in render/mount, and for in-app navigation use runtime registration of exact paths (a legitimate use of the public register API — it\'s designed for \\\"后续板块模块可安全覆盖骨架占位页\\\"). Runtime registration of exact paths is within the public contract and doesn\'t modify skeleton files.\\n\\nFor direct-hash entry: I\'ll add a small self-registration step at script load: for each existing knowledge item, register its exact path. Combined with runtime registration on click, both paths work. For unknown ids typed directly (like \'#/study/knowledge/nonexistent\'), 404 page shows — acceptable edge case.\\n\\nHmm wait, actually, let me reconsider once more whether I can do better for direct hash entry. What if my study.js script itself listens to hashchange before the router? No — router also listens. Order matters; router renders on hashchange. If I registered routes for all knowledge ids at load time, direct hash entry works for all stored ids (including seed). That covers the acceptance criterion (seed data + persisted). Good enough.\\n\\nActually — even better idea! I can register the DETAIL definition under a wide net: since the router only has exact match + \'*\' fallback, and \'*\' is already registered by app.js as 404... I can\'t override \'*\'. \\n\\nHmm, but wait: \\\"同名路径重复注册时，后者覆盖前者（板块模块可安全覆盖骨架占位页）\\\". \'*\'\' is the 404 fallback registered by app.js. If my script registers \'*\' with my own definition... that would override the 404 page for ALL unknown paths — that would break the 404 page and potentially interfere with other agents\' expectations. Bad idea. Don\'t touch \'*\'.\\n\\nSo final approach for knowledge detail:\\n1. Register \'/study/knowledge/:id\' literally with detail definition (contract compliance; render/mount parse the id from path — path would literally be \'/study/knowledge/:id\' when that route renders; parse \':id\' segment → id=\':id\'... hmm, that\'s broken. Let me think about what render(path) receives: path = parsed hash. For route \'/study/knowledge/:id\', render receives path = \'/study/knowledge/:id\' (the literal string as it was navigated). So parsing the last segment gives \':id\' — not a real id. This literal registration is basically a placeholder that satisfies the letter of the requirement.\\n\\nActually hmm, is that even useful? Let me think about the best interpretation:\\n\\nThe task says \\\"必须实现的页面及要求：3. \'/study/knowledge/:id\' 知识点详情（动态路径需处理 id）\\\" — the requirement is the DETAIL PAGE must exist and handle a dynamic id. The most sensible implementation: detail page definition as a function that renders based on an id extracted from path. Registration:\\n- Literal \'/study/knowledge/:id\' — satisfies \\\"通过 registerPage 注册\\\".\\n- Runtime: register exact paths for each knowledge item (at load + on open) with the same definition.\\n\\nIn the detail definition\'s render/mount, extract id: `path.split(\'/\').pop()` and decode. When the literal route \'/study/knowledge/:id\' renders (only if someone navigates to the literal string), id = \':id\' → show empty state \\\"未找到知识点\\\" gracefully.\\n\\nFor navigation from tree/list/detail→questions: use exact registered paths.\\n\\nOK that\'s my plan for the dynamic route. Same approach for questions \\\"定位到该题\\\": navigate to \'/study/questions\' and use a module-level `pendingQuestionId` variable consumed in mount (scroll + expand). Direct hash entry isn\'t required for question focus — \\\"点击跳转题库并定位到该题\\\" is an in-app interaction.\\n\\nWait, actually, for question focus I could also use \'#/study/questions/<id>\'... but simpler: pending variable. But hold on — App.navigate(\'/study/questions\') — if current page IS \'/study/questions\', navigate re-renders (same hash → render()), mount runs again and reads pendingQuestionId. Good.\\n\\nNow — one more consideration about registerPage timing. app.js loads pages via index.html: `<script src=\\\"js/pages/study.js\\\">` presumably after app.js. app.js registers global pages at load; boot on DOMContentLoaded. pages/*.js register at load. So window.App exists when study.js runs (app.js IIFE executes immediately). But index.html doesn\'t exist yet — other agent creating it. To be safe, I\'ll guard registration: if window.App exists → register now; else wait for DOMContentLoaded and retry (with interval fallback).\\n\\nAlso index.html may not include study.js at all... it should, since the task says \\\"浏览器直接打开 index.html 后可通过侧边栏进入上述每个页面\\\" and sidebar contains 考公区 sub-nav items (paths like /study/knowledge etc. — see app.js SEARCH_SOURCES referencing \'/study/knowledge\', \'/study/questions\', \'/study/wrong\', \'/study/plans\', \'/study/checkin\', \'/study/shizheng\').\\n\\nInteresting! app.js search references the paths: \'/study/knowledge\', \'/study/questions\', \'/study/wrong\', \'/study/plans\', \'/study/checkin\', \'/study/shizheng\'. Note: \'/study/checkin\' (not \'/study/clock\'!). And the sidebar will likely use these same paths. My task says register: \'/study\', \'/study/knowledge\', \'/study/knowledge/:id\', \'/study/questions\', \'/study/wrong\', \'/study/plan\', \'/study/clock\', \'/study/current\'.\\n\\nHmm — conflict: task says \'/study/plan\', \'/study/clock\', \'/study/current\', but app.js search uses \'/study/plans\', \'/study/checkin\', \'/study/shizheng\'. The task is explicit about the paths to register: \'/study/plan\' 学习计划, \'/study/clock\' 学习打卡, \'/study/current\' 时政积累. But to be consistent with the app shell (search + likely sidebar), I should ALSO register the aliases \'/study/plans\', \'/study/checkin\', \'/study/shizheng\' pointing to the same definitions. That way both navigation paths work. The task says \\\"必须实现的页面\\\" with those paths; registering extra aliases doesn\'t violate anything (\\\"只创建和修改 js/pages/study.js 一个文件\\\" — all within study.js).\\n\\nI\'ll register:\\n- \'/study\' (考公区总览)\\n- \'/study/knowledge\' (知识点树)\\n- \'/study/knowledge/:id\' (详情, literal + runtime exact registration)\\n- \'/study/questions\' (题库)\\n- \'/study/wrong\' (错题本)\\n- \'/study/plan\' + \'/study/plans\' (学习计划)\\n- \'/study/clock\' + \'/study/checkin\' (学习打卡)\\n- \'/study/current\' + \'/study/shizheng\' (时政积累)\\n\\nSidebar items likely use \'/study/plans\', \'/study/checkin\', \'/study/shizheng\' (consistent with search paths). I\'ll use the aliases in my own internal navigation to be consistent with the shell (search results navigate to those paths). Actually for my internal links, I\'ll use the canonical paths from the task (\'/study/plan\', \'/study/clock\', \'/study/current\') — hmm, but search navigates to \'/study/plans\' etc. Both registered → both work. For my own data-nav attributes, I\'ll use the task-specified paths. Both fine.\\n\\nWait, also home page \'开始打卡\' button → data-nav=\\\"/study/checkin\\\" (from app.js line 402). So \'/study/checkin\' must resolve to clock page. Good — alias registered.\\n\\nNow let me check index.html existence again — maybe it appeared. Also check whether other pages/*.js exist (work.js, personal.js) to match style conventions (module pattern, CSS injection approach).\",\"content\":\"契约已完全明确：路由是精确匹配，`render(path)/mount(el, path)` 会收到完整路径。我再看是否有 index.html 与其他页面模块（了解平行协作者的代码风格与命名惯例）。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"契约已完全明确：路由是精确匹配，`render(path)/mount(el, path)` 会收到完整路径。我再看是否有 index.html 与其他页面模块（了解平行协作者的代码风格与命名惯例）。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":11,\"round\":11,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":11,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:21:26'),
