(1033, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 138358, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'skeleton', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"skeleton-turn-21\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Almost everything passes. The only failure: 工作区占位页 missing \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" text. Why? The page should render \'/work\' placeholder... Wait — maybe the issue: my check for \\\"/work\\\" page — the dump loaded `#/work`... The title contains 工作区 (PASS — check said \\\"工作区\\\" present? Actually the FAIL line only shows missing \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\"). Hmm, \\\"工作区\\\" was found (not in missing list). So the /work page rendered — but \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" is missing?\\n\\nWait — look at work.js placeholder: `<p>今日待办、收件箱、项目、日志与会议等页面将在后续任务中实现</p>`. The substring \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" should be present... unless the mount replaced content? Or the check string differs — in the HTML: \\\"等页面将在后续任务中实现\\\" — substring \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" IS contained. Hmm.\\n\\nWait, maybe the page didn\'t render because... `if (window.App)` guard — App exists. Actually maybe the issue is the anchor: `#/work` — hmm wait, in the dump, I passed URL `index + \\\"#/work\\\"`. Chrome file URL with fragment. The router parses \'#/work\' → \'/work\'. The placeholder registered in work.js. Should render.\\n\\nBut \\\"工作区\\\" found — that could be from the sidebar nav (工作区 text always in sidebar!). So maybe the /work placeholder page did NOT render, and the sidebar just has 工作区 text. What would have rendered then? 404 page! Because... hmm, why would \'/work\' fall to 404?\\n\\nOh wait! I see. In work.js I have:\\n\\n```js\\nif (window.App) {\\n  App.registerPage(\'/work\', {...});\\n}\\n```\\n\\nApp is a global const declared in app.js IIFE? No — `window.App = {...}` assigned via `var App = {...}` inside IIFE then... wait, in app.js: `var App = {...}` — that\'s local to the IIFE! Did I attach it to window? Let me check... In app.js I wrote `var App = { ... }` and at the end `window.App`? Let me re-check: I wrote at top \\\"window.App 提供\\\" in comments, and the App object is created as `var App = {...}` inside the IIFE, and... hmm, do I do `window.App = App` anywhere?\\n\\nLooking at my app.js code: I don\'t see `window.App = App;`! I created `var App` and registered pages via `App.registerPage` — but never attached App to window! That means js/pages/*.js `if (window.App)` is FALSE → no pages registered → \'/work\' → 404.\\n\\nBut wait — home/settings/search pages DID render (tests passed!). Because those are registered inside app.js IIFE where `App` is in scope. And sidebar stuff works. But `window.App` is undefined!\\n\\nThat\'s a critical bug for the contract — later page modules depend on `window.App`. Must fix: add `window.App = App;` before the IIFE closes.\\n\\nAlso explains why work.js placeholder didn\'t register: `window.App` undefined.\\n\\nFix: in app.js, right before `})();` at the end (or right after creating App), add `window.App = App;`. Best after all App methods defined (they\'re defined on the object progressively). Actually App.theme etc. are assigned after the object literal — so window.App must be set after all assignments. Put it right before the boot function or at end of IIFE. Let me add `window.App = App;` just before `function boot()` or after boot definition at end. I\'ll add right before the final `})();`.\\n\\nLet me also double-check other contract points:\\n- router.js: window.WorkbenchRouter assigned ✓\\n- store.js: window.WorkbenchStore assigned ✓\\n\\nFix now.\",\"content\":\"发现关键缺陷：app.js 内部创建了 `App` 对象并完成所有挂载，但从未赋值给 `window.App`，导致页面模块无法通过 `window.App` 访问契约（工作区占位页因此未注册而落入 404）。立即修复：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"发现关键缺陷：app.js 内部创建了 `App` 对象并完成所有挂载，但从未赋值给 `window.App`，导致页面模块无法通过 `window.App` 访问契约（工作区占位页因此未注册而落入 404）。立即修复：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":21,\"round\":21,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":21,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:44:10'),
(1034, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 138359, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_work', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_work-turn-21\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"命令被预检拦截。用 read_file 直接读文件确认（read_file 是安全的）。先读文件末尾部分看看内容是否正确写入，顺便确认行号。\",\"content\":\"改用 read_file 直接确认文件状态与关键代码位置：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"改用 read_file 直接确认文件状态与关键代码位置：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":21,\"round\":21,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":21,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:44:10'),
(1035, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 138360, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-21\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Syntax + stub load test PASS — 13 routes registered including dynamic knowledge routes.\\n\\nNow: run a deeper functional test in a simulated DOM environment. The best approach: use jsdom if available (unlikely without npm install — no external installs allowed? Installing packages via npm would modify node_modules — but that\'s in temp dir, not the project. However \\\"无外部资源\\\" applies to the web app; test tooling can use whatever. But npm install jsdom may take time/network. Let me check if jsdom is available globally or in some shared location.\\n\\nAlternative: extend my stub harness to simulate DOM enough to run render/mount for each page and assert key behaviors:\\n- Call each registered definition\'s render(path) and check HTML contains expected markers.\\n- Simulate store with seed data.\\n- Call mount with a fake el (with querySelector returning stubs...). mount is complex — needs many querySelector results. A full functional DOM test without jsdom is too heavy.\\n\\nBetter: check if jsdom exists somewhere (e.g., global npm). Let me try `node -e \\\"require(\'jsdom\')\\\"` — if not found, skip; the stub-level test plus careful review may suffice. Actually, let me try a quick npm-based check in temp dir: `npm ls -g jsdom` or just try require from a temp dir.\\n\\nActually — another pragmatic approach: build a minimal DOM shim sufficient for the pages. That\'s a lot of work but gives real coverage of render() (pure string building) and mount() (event binding). The render functions are pure HTML strings — I can at least invoke each render() with a real-ish store and validate the HTML output contains key markers and that store interactions work (e.g., openNewPlanModal is closure-private...).\\n\\nGiven the render functions are the most complex string-building parts (template literals), testing them with a store stub is valuable: they\'d catch runtime errors like undefined vars, missing functions, template mistakes. The mount functions need DOM. I could test render() only for all 13 paths, plus test parseQuestions indirectly? parseQuestions is closure-private... but render for questions page doesn\'t call it.\\n\\nLet me write harness2 that:\\n1. Loads study.js with stubs where store has REAL data (seed-like arrays + real CRUD on plain objects).\\n2. Captures registrations with definitions.\\n3. For each path, calls def.render(path) and asserts:\\n   - returns string of length > 0\\n   - no \'undefined\' literal in output (would indicate broken template vars) — careful: \'undefined\' could legitimately appear in text? Unlikely in my copy. I\'ll check for \'undefined\' and \'NaN\' tokens.\\n4. Simulates some store operations: questions.add → verify list length grows; planProgress-like logic? closure-private.\\n\\nrender() calls functions like overviewStats (uses store.checkins.list etc.), treeState (getUI → settings.studyUI — need settings object), knCardHTML (fmtDue etc.), DETAIL_DEF.render (store.knowledge.get), QUESTIONS_DEF.render (store.questions.list), WRONG_DEF.render, PLAN_DEF.render (planCardHTML etc.), CLOCK_DEF.render (clockState → settings.studyClock), SHIZHENG_DEF.render.\\n\\nMy stub store needs real list implementations + get + add/update that actually mutate arrays. Let me build that.\\n\\nFor path \'/study/knowledge/seed-know-1\' render — detailIdFromPath(path) — path passed directly, fine.\\n\\nAlso for the detail path with unknown id (\'/study/knowledge/nope\') → renders not-found branch — test too.\\n\\nAlso PLAN_DEF.render uses getUI().planView — settings.studyUI undefined → getUI returns {} → view \'week\'. OK.\\n\\nrenderChart is called in mount only.\\n\\nLet me also check CLOCK_DEF.render: clockState → settings.studyClock undefined → defaults. fmtHM etc fine. streakDays uses checkins list.\\n\\nI\'ll write harness2 with mutable store and run renders for all paths, assert no exceptions and no \'undefined\'/\'NaN\' tokens.\\n\\nAdditionally test dynamic behaviors I can reach through render only — e.g., overview with data → numbers appear.\\n\\nThen also do a jsdom attempt: check availability first. Let me check `npm root -g` and whether jsdom installed globally. Quick: `node -e \\\"try{require(\'jsdom\');console.log(\'jsdom OK\')}catch(e){console.log(\'no jsdom\')}\\\"`.\\n\\nLet me do that in the act run along with harness2. Actually keep phases clean: create harness2 file first (create_file), then run.\",\"content\":\"语法与注册测试通过。现在编写更深的渲染级测试（真实 store 桩 + 全部页面 render 冒烟），并检查 jsdom 是否可用做完整 DOM 测试。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"语法与注册测试通过。现在编写更深的渲染级测试（真实 store 桩 + 全部页面 render 冒烟），并检查 jsdom 是否可用做完整 DOM 测试。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":21,\"round\":21,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":21,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:44:10'),
