(1073, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 144959, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'skeleton', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"skeleton-turn-23\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Interesting — work.js and study.js placeholders still fail, but personal.js passes. Why?\\n\\nHmm, personal.js has the same structure... wait, the difference: study.js and work.js — let me think. What\'s different between them?\\n\\nwork.js: `App.registerPage(\'/work\', ...)` — registered. But \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" missing while \\\"工作区\\\" found (from sidebar). So \'/work\' fell to 404? But personal passed...\\n\\nWait — maybe the issue is the text. Let me look: work.js says `\'<p>今日待办、收件箱、项目、日志与会议等页面将在后续任务中实现</p>\'`. Substring check: \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" — should match...\\n\\nUnless... the mount click handler? No.\\n\\nHold on — maybe the placeholder page DID render but Chrome dump encodes something? No, personal worked.\\n\\nWait, actually — maybe the issue: \'/work\' IS registered (window.App now exists, personal works so App works). Hmm, but personal.js loads AFTER study.js which loads after work.js. All three use `if (window.App)`. If window.App existed, all three register. Unless... window.App assignment happens in app.js boot section — `window.App = App;` executes immediately when app.js runs (it\'s at IIFE top level, before boot). Yes it\'s synchronous. So all three should register.\\n\\nHmm wait — did my edit to app.js actually get placed correctly? The edit inserted `window.App = App;` before `function boot()`. It said lines_changed [900,902]. Let me verify app.js syntax still OK and the line exists. But personal.js passing suggests App exists (otherwise personal would also fail).\\n\\nSo why would work.js and study.js placeholders fail while personal passes?\\n\\nOH WAIT. I see it! The check strings: For personal I checked [\\\"随笔区\\\", \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\"]. For study: [\\\"考公区\\\", \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\"] — study.js says \'<p>知识点、题库、错题、计划、打卡与时政等页面将在后续任务中实现</p>\'. Hmm substring present.\\n\\nHmm, but wait — the DUMP: for /work I passed fragment \\\"#/work\\\". But look at the check — \\\"工作区\\\" WAS found... but that\'s in the sidebar. So /work page didn\'t render its placeholder.\\n\\nIs it possible that the check for \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" failed because of the actual page rendering the 404? But then why personal OK?\\n\\nLet me think about script load order: store, router, app, pages/work, pages/study, pages/personal. If work.js threw an error (syntax?), the remaining scripts still run. But node --check passed all.\\n\\nHmm — maybe there\'s a subtle issue: In work.js and study.js I used `App.registerPage(\'/work\', {...})` — same as personal. \\n\\nWait wait. Let me recheck the HTML output difference. Maybe the issue is the em-dash or specific characters... no.\\n\\nActually — let me reconsider: personal.js check passed. work.js failed on \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" only. Could the /work placeholder render but with different text? Let me dump the actual content of #/work and grep. Let me debug: dump DOM for #/work and print the content div. Perhaps the mount replaced content? No, mount just adds click listener.\\n\\nHmm, another thought: \'/work\' might be shadowed by... the 404 fallback? No — fallback only used when no exact match. \'/work\' IS registered by work.js...\\n\\nUNLESS work.js didn\'t run because of an earlier script error! If pages/work.js threw during load, study.js and personal.js... wait personal passed. So personal.js ran. If work.js errored, study.js would still run (separate script tags). So work+study failing together while personal passes — what do work and study have in common that personal doesn\'t?\\n\\nwork.js title \'工作区\', study.js title \'考公区\', personal.js title \'随笔区\'. Hmm... \\n\\nOH! I think I see it! In work.js and study.js, the render function contains `\'    \' + App.icon(\'work\', 44) +` and `App.icon(\'study\', 44)`. And personal: `App.icon(\'personal\', 44)`. All fine...\\n\\nHmm, what about the HTML content check: is \\\"将在后续任务中实现\\\" actually in the rendered output? Maybe the dump truncated? No.\\n\\nLet me actually debug by dumping the #content innerHTML for /work. Also check whether the /work route hit 404 (which would include \\\"尚未注册\\\"). Let me print the relevant slice of the dumped DOM.\",\"content\":\"personal 占位通过而 work/study 未通过，需要调试。直接 dump `#/work` 的正文内容查看实际渲染结果：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"personal 占位通过而 work/study 未通过，需要调试。直接 dump `#/work` 的正文内容查看实际渲染结果：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":23,\"round\":23,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":23,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:45:48'),
