(1149, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 151889, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'skeleton', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"skeleton-turn-27\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Excellent findings:\\n\\n1. work.js and study.js use ONLY my documented contract APIs: registerPage, navigate, refresh, store (collections + settings + updateSettings + subscribe), showToast, openModal, icon, escapeHtml, uid (maybe), formatDate (maybe). The grep (truncated) shows no usage of undefined APIs so far.\\n\\n2. Important compatibility notes from their comments:\\n   - work.js line 13: \\\"骨架 App.openModal 的回调语义为「先关闭弹窗再调用 onConfirm」\\\" — matches my implementation (confirm click → closeModal() then onConfirm(closeModal)). \\n   - study.js line 861: `App.openModal(\'<div>\' + opts + \'</div>\', {...})` — passes options object as second arg. My implementation handles that ✓. It uses {onConfirm, ...} presumably with confirmText etc. — my opts handling covers title/confirmText/cancelText/hideCancel/onConfirm/onCancel/closeOnMask ✓.\\n   - study.js uses `App.store.settings.studyUI / studyClock` namespaces via updateSettings — my updateSettings merges shallowly into settings object, so arbitrary keys work ✓. BUT: my importJSON and clearAll... clearAll keeps settings (fine). importJSON REPLACES settings with only theme/fontSize/sidebarCollapsed — studyClock/studyUI lost on import. Acceptable (import is a full restore).\\n   - study.js `App.store.plans.list().filter(p => p.status !== \'done\')` — my seed plans lack `status` field! My plans seed: {type, title, start, end, modules, progress, createdAt} — no status. study.js expects status (\'active\'/\'done\'). Their overview filters `p.status !== \'done\'` — undefined !== \'done\' → true, so seed plans show as active. OK no break. But when they update/add plans, they set status. Fine.\\n   - study.js checkins: they `find(c => c.date === today)` and UPDATE existing — my seed checkins have a today record (55 min). Fine.\\n   - study.js line 484: plans filter — fine.\\n   - study.js knowledge: they filter by path etc. My knowledge seed has \'path\' field ✓ (they use k.path? line 238: `App.store.knowledge.list().filter(function (k) {` — likely filters by path prefix. My seed paths: \'行测 > 言语理解 > 逻辑填空\' — with spaces around \'>\'. If they match exact path strings like \'行测>言语理解>逻辑填空\' (no spaces), filtering would fail and the tree would show empty! Hmm. Let me check how study.js builds the tree and what path format it expects. This matters because my seed data must integrate with their pages.\\n\\n   Also mastery: study.js uses MASTERY_NAMES[level-1] — mastery values 0-4 or 1-5? I set mastery: 3, 2, 1, 1. They do `mastery: level` where level presumably 1-5 and MASTERY_NAMES[level-1]. My seed 1-3 fits (未学→了解→掌握). OK.\\n   \\n   - study.js questions: expects {module, stem, options, answer, analysis, source, tags} — my seed matches ✓. Tags as array ✓.\\n   - wrongQuestions: {questionId, reason, reviewCount, lastResult, status, nextReview} — my seed has these ✓ (status \'pending\'/\'learning\'/\'archived\').\\n   - shizheng: {title, source, date, summary, insight, quote, tags} ✓.\\n   - plans: they filter status; my seeds lack status → treated active. Also plans progress number ✓.\\n   - checkins: {date, durationMin, modules, summary} ✓.\\n\\n3. The main risk area: knowledge path format. Let me check study.js\'s tree logic — how it derives 科目/模块 from k.path. Let me grep study.js for path parsing.\\n\\nAlso work.js:\\n- todos: {title, quadrant, priority, due, done, projectId, createdAt} ✓ — they also use completedAt (update with completedAt) — fine, extra field.\\n- inbox: {text, urgency, done, createdAt} ✓\\n- projects: {name, desc, color, status, createdAt} — they use status \'active\'/\'archived\'/\'paused\' and sort field. My seed has status active/paused ✓, no sort — fine.\\n- logs: {date, content, autoGen?} ✓\\n- meetings: {title, datetime, attendees, summary, decisions, todos?} ✓\\n\\n4. work.js registers \'/work/projects/:id\' literal + dynamic registration — fine with my exact-match router? Their comment says \\\"字面占位，实际由动态注册接管\\\" — they dynamically register \'/work/projects/<id>\' when navigating. My router does exact matching, so dynamic registration works. But if a user directly opens \'#/work/projects/seed-proj-1\' before dynamic registration... the literal \':id\' won\'t match. That\'s their design decision; fine.\\n\\nNow let me verify the knowledge path format compatibility — grep study.js for how it parses path.\",\"content\":\"并行模块全部只使用我文档化的契约 API（registerPage/navigate/refresh/store/showToast/openModal/icon/escapeHtml），且 openModal 的对象式调用与我实现一致。还需确认关键兼容点：study.js 对 knowledge 的 path 字段格式的解析方式，以及 seed 数据字段是否匹配：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"并行模块全部只使用我文档化的契约 API（registerPage/navigate/refresh/store/showToast/openModal/icon/escapeHtml），且 openModal 的对象式调用与我实现一致。还需确认关键兼容点：study.js 对 knowledge 的 path 字段格式的解析方式，以及 seed 数据字段是否匹配：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":27,\"round\":27,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":27,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:49:32'),
(1150, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 151890, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_work', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_work-turn-27\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"现在修改 mount 的 tab 点击处理为局部更新（保留指示器滑动动画）。原文：\\n\\n```js\\n        var tabBtn = e.target.closest(\'.work-tab[data-tab]\');\\n        if (tabBtn) {\\n          self._tab = tabBtn.getAttribute(\'data-tab\');\\n          refreshWorkPage();\\n          return;\\n        }\\n```\\n\\n改为局部更新：\\n```js\\n        var tabBtn = e.target.closest(\'.work-tab[data-tab]\');\\n        if (tabBtn) {\\n          var nextTab = tabBtn.getAttribute(\'data-tab\');\\n          if (nextTab === self._tab) return;\\n          self._tab = nextTab;\\n          /* 复用 Tab 元素：下划线滑动 + 面板局部替换 */\\n          $$(\'.work-tab\', el).forEach(function (t) {\\n            t.classList.toggle(\'active\', t === tabBtn);\\n          });\\n          var indicator = $(\'.work-tab-indicator\', el);\\n          if (indicator) {\\n            indicator.style.width = tabBtn.offsetWidth + \'px\';\\n            indicator.style.transform = \'translateX(\' + tabBtn.offsetLeft + \'px)\';\\n          }\\n          var panel = $(\'[data-act=\\\"panel\\\"]\', el);\\n          if (panel) {\\n            var tmp = document.createElement(\'div\');\\n            tmp.innerHTML = detailPanelHtml(self._id, nextTab);\\n            panel.innerHTML = tmp.firstElementChild ? tmp.firstElementChild.outerHTML : \'\';\\n          }\\n          return;\\n        }\\n```\",\"content\":\"修改 mount 中 Tab 切换为局部更新（保留滑动指示器动画）：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"修改 mount 中 Tab 切换为局部更新（保留滑动指示器动画）：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":27,\"round\":27,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":27,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:49:32'),
(1151, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 151891, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-27\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Preflight blocks `node -e` in inspect (dynamic). I\'ll check jsdom availability within an act-phase command. Combine with next steps: act = check jsdom + (if available) run a jsdom-based interaction test. But the interaction test file needs writing first — let me write harness3 (jsdom-based) now, then run act: `node -e check jsdom` first... Actually simpler: write harness3 that requires jsdom and if missing prints SKIP with exit 0. Then act runs `node harness3.js`; if jsdom exists it runs full tests.\\n\\nharness3 design (jsdom):\\n- jsdom global setup: `const { JSDOM } = require(\'jsdom\'); const dom = new JSDOM(\'<!DOCTYPE html><html><body><div id=\\\"content\\\"></div><div id=\\\"modal-root\\\"></div><div id=\\\"toast-root\\\"></div><div id=\\\"sidebar\\\"></div><div id=\\\"topbar-title\\\"></div></body></html>\', { url: \'http://localhost/\', pretendToBeVisual: true });`\\n- set global.window = dom.window; global.document = dom.window.document; also copy window properties needed (location, requestAnimationFrame, localStorage? store stub doesn\'t need localStorage — I\'m stubbing store directly, not loading store.js).\\n- Actually simpler: load study.js with jsdom globals and a real-ish store stub (reuse harness2\'s store), then:\\n  - For each page: def.render(path) → set content.innerHTML = html → def.mount(contentEl, path) → run interactions:\\n    - /study: click entry card data-nav → assert App.navigate called with path (stub records).\\n    - /study/knowledge: click a node row (data-select), assert list updates (content changes); type search? set input value + dispatchEvent(\'input\') → wait 300ms → assert list filtered. That requires timers — use real setTimeout with async await.\\n    - /study/questions: mount → assert listBox children > 0; click toggle → expand; click answer → mask removed.\\n    - /study/wrong: mount → click item → review panel appears; click option → result banner appears.\\n    - /study/plan: mount → chart bars present; click plan card → detail expands.\\n    - /study/clock: mount → timer display; click start → running; click pause; submit? (elapsed < 1min → toast warn — hard to assert without DOM toast; skip or check state text).\\n    - /study/current: mount → list present; click prev → month changes.\\n    - detail k1: mount → click mastery pill opens modal (modal-root child added); click collapse head toggles open.\\n  - unmount each after.\\n\\njsdom events: element.click() works (dispatchEvent). querySelectorAll returns NodeList with forEach. classList works. hidden property works. style.setProperty works. innerHTML parsing works. requestAnimationFrame: pretendToBeVisual gives rAF.\\n\\nTimers: use setTimeout — real. My debounce is 250ms; tests can await 350ms.\\n\\nlocalStorage: not needed since store stub.\\n\\nwindow.App stub — same as harness2 but navigate records paths.\\n\\ndocument.getElementById(\'content\') — jsdom document with those ids.\\n\\nThe mount functions reference document.getElementById(\'content\') for unmount cleanup (el._unsub etc.) — works with jsdom.\\n\\nFor /study/questions focus flow: openQuestion sets pendingFocus and calls App.navigate — not directly testable via mount (it\'s internal). Skip.\\n\\nFor /study/knowledge tree: initial render selected 行测; list shows k2 (行测 > 言语理解 > 逻辑填空 — wait, selected [\'行测\'] → knowledgeForNode([\'行测\']) → k1,k2 (both start with 行测) → 2 cards. Click on node \'行测/判断推理/图形推理\' → list shows k1 only. Good assertion.\\n\\nSearch: set input value \'申论\' dispatch input → await 350ms → list contains k3 title.\\n\\nFor wrong: click w1 item (pending) → review panel; options: q1 has 4 options; click first option (\'A\' correct) → result banner \'答对了\' & updated: consecutive 0→1, status learning, nextReview +2 days; verify store update. Then click 下一题 → next pending... only w1 pending; queue = [w1]; after w1, reviewIdx=1 → \'本组复习完成\'. Good.\\n\\nAlso test wrong answer path: click wrong option letter → status pending, nextReview = today+1.\\n\\nFor clock: mount → display \'00:00:00\'; click start → running state; advance: can\'t wait real time — but display refresh uses clockElapsed with startedAt now — after 1100ms, elapsed ~1s → display \'00:00:01\'. Await 1.2s and assert display != \'00:00:00\'. Then pause. Then click reset → \'00:00:00\'. Submit with <1min → toast called with warn (stub records toasts) — assert last toast type \'warn\'. Then to test submit success we\'d need ≥1 min — skip (or set accumulated by manipulating settings? clockElapsed reads settings.studyClock — I can set settings.studyClock = {running:false, startedAt:0, accumulated: 61000, modules:[]} then click submit → checkin added! Since mount reads state fresh each refresh() call from clockState() → reads App.store.settings.studyClock → updated. submitBtn handler reads clockElapsed(st) — st is the local object captured at mount... Hmm, st local var is initialized at mount from clockState() and mutated by handlers. If I modify settings.studyClock externally, local st won\'t see it. So instead simulate: click start, wait ~1.1s, click pause (accumulated ~1s), then directly set st? Not accessible. Alternative: wait 61 seconds — too long.\\n\\nAlternative: test submit success via pre-seeding: before mount, set settings.studyClock = {running:false, startedAt:0, accumulated: 61000, modules:[\'言语理解\']} → mount reads st with accumulated 61000 → refresh shows 1:01 → click submit → checkin merged with today +1min → assert checkins store has today record with durationMin increased; toast success. That works! And module chips: chipsBox has \'言语理解\' active.\\n\\nNote: merging with existing seed checkin c1 (today 55min) → durationMin becomes 56. Assert store.checkins.list() today record durationMin === 56.\\n\\nFor plan: mount auto-updates progress & possibly marks done. p1: week plan start -1 end +5, target 5h=300min; checkins in range: c1(55, today within range) + c2(120, -1 in range) = 175 → progress 58%. Assert chart bars exist, plan card exists. Click card → detail visible (hidden false). Also test new plan modal? openNewPlanModal closure-private; skip modal open (it\'s triggered by button click → App.openModal called with html — assert modal-root innerHTML contains \'新建计划\'? openModal is my stub recording html. Actually openModal stub in harness2 returns makeEl; in harness3 I want real modal? Simpler: stub openModal to record html string into a var. Click \'#st-plan-new\' → assert recorded html contains \'计划类型\'. Good.\\n\\nSame for questions add/import buttons and shizheng add — assert modal html recorded.\\n\\nFor detail page: mount(\'/study/knowledge/k1\'): click \'#st-mastery-pill\' → modal recorded with 5 options; simulate choosing level 5: my modal flow relies on App.openModal returning mask to query — with stub openModal returning a real element? If I stub openModal to return a jsdom element (document.createElement(\'div\')) and store html via innerHTML, then mask.querySelector works on it. I can then: mask.querySelector(\'input[name=\\\"mastery\\\"][value=\\\"5\\\"]\').checked = true... but my code\'s onConfirm reads checked from mask. The confirm click is handled by app.js\'s openModal (not available). In my stub openModal I record html and return the created element; onConfirm stored; I can invoke onConfirm(closeFn) manually. Let me implement stub:\\n\\n```js\\nvar modalState = { html: \'\', onConfirm: null, mask: null, closeCalled: false };\\nwindow.App.openModal = function (html, opts) {\\n  var mask = document.createElement(\'div\');\\n  mask.innerHTML = html;\\n  modalState.html = html; modalState.mask = mask;\\n  if (typeof opts === \'function\') modalState.onConfirm = opts;\\n  else modalState.onConfirm = opts.onConfirm;\\n  return mask;\\n};\\n```\\nThen tests can call modalState.onConfirm(function(){modalState.closeCalled=true;}) after setting radio states. But note my mastery modal code calls `mask.querySelectorAll(\'.st-mastery-opt\').forEach(...)` right after openModal — mask is a jsdom div with innerHTML → works.\\n\\nFor plan modal onConfirm reads mask.querySelector(\'input[data-mod]\') etc. — works with real element + innerHTML.\\n\\nQuestion add modal: mask.querySelector(\'#f-stem\').value — innerHTML creates input elements; setting .value works. Then onConfirm(close) → store.questions.add → assert count.\\n\\nOK this is getting substantial but valuable. Let me also test:\\n- setRoll presence: overview mount → .st-roll elements get data-val updated to target after setRoll. Assert data-val === target.\\n\\nTime to write harness3. It\'s long; let me write carefully with async/await (node 24 supports).\\n\\nKey detail: study.js load — needs window.App at load; set globals before require.\\n\\nAlso document.body classList used by reading mode. jsdom supports classList on elements. \\n\\nOne concern: study.js unmount functions use `document.getElementById(\'content\')` and read el._unsub — fine.\\n\\nAlso TREE_DEF mount: `el.querySelector(\'#st-tree-pane\')` etc. — content element must contain rendered HTML. I\'ll do: contentEl.innerHTML = def.render(path); then def.mount(contentEl, path).\\n\\nAfter mount, find elements via contentEl.querySelector.\\n\\nFor clock page mount: it calls `saveClockState(st)` only on user actions; initial refresh() sets display. Note: clock mount\'s auto-clamp: st.startedAt must be same-day for our seed (startedAt 0 → not running → no clamp). Good.\\n\\nCareful with clock submit: st local init at mount reads settings.studyClock — I set it BEFORE mount. Then submit uses clockElapsed(st) = accumulated 61000 → mins=1 → merge with today\'s checkin → durationMin 56. Assert. Then reset state persisted: settings.studyClock.accumulated === 0. Good.\\n\\nNote CLOCK_DEF.mount queries \'#st-clock-start\' etc by id — render has those ids. Good.\\n\\nAlso chips: render has chips with data-mod; mount adds active class for st.modules — modules [\'言语理解\'] → chip active. click chip toggles.\\n\\nNow for the wrong page test: WRONG_DEF.mount binds listBox click. After mount, listBox has 3 items (w1 pending, w2 learning, w3 archived). Click w1 (data-review=w1) → enterReview → reviewBox visible with options. Click option \'A\' (correct) → result banner. Assert store.update applied: w1 status \'learning\', consecutive 1, reviewCount 2, nextReview today+2. Assert banner contains \'答对了\'. Then click next → \'本组复习完成\' (queue was [w1] only... wait queue built from all non-archived sorted: w1(pending, nextReview today), w2(learning, today+2) → queue [w1, w2]. After w1 → reviewIdx 1 → w2 renders. Click option on w2: q2 options A,B; correct A. w2 consecutive 1→2 → status learning, nextReview +4 days. Then next → reviewIdx 2 → no more → \'本组复习完成\'. \\n\\nAlso test wrong answer: click w2 again? After exiting... simpler separate: click item w1 again (fresh) → choose option \'B\' (wrong) → banner \'答错了\', status pending, nextReview today+1. Good.\\n\\nBut careful: after first review round, w1 status learning; list re-rendered on exitReview. For second round, click w1 item again — data-review attr still w1. enterReview finds w1 in queue (non-archived) — fine.\\n\\nAlso wrong item click requires item element — after exitReview renderList() re-renders; need to re-query elements. I\'ll structure tests sequentially with fresh queries.\\n\\nAlso the tab switch test: click \'待复习\' tab → list only w1-ish pending items.\\n\\nOK also for knowledge search test — debounce 250ms: await sleep(400).\\n\\nLet me now write harness3. Also include route render via all defs like harness2 quickly (skip—already done).\\n\\nAdditionally, one more important runtime check: **router.js interplay** — I\'m not loading router/app/store (stubbed). The real app does exact matching; my registrations are verified. Fine.\\n\\nPotential issue I should double check in code: DETAIL_DEF.mount uses `el.querySelector(\'#st-mastery-pill\') ? ... : detailIdFromPath(location.hash)` — location exists in jsdom (url set). OK.\\n\\nAnother: TREE_DEF mount refreshList uses search.value — jsdom input value works.\\n\\nAlso for /study/knowledge mount: subscribe stub returns noop; el._unsub set. Fine.\\n\\nPlan mount: `el.querySelector(\'#st-plan-seg\')` etc. Chart renderChart called → box.innerHTML set with bars; then rAF sets heights. rAF available with pretendToBeVisual. Assert .st-chart-bar count > 0 (they\'re in innerHTML after renderChart).\\n\\nAlso plan auto-progress update: assert store.plans.get(\'p1\').progress === 58 (175/300=58.33→58). Wait: actualMin=175, target=300 → 58.33 → round 58. Assert 58.\\n\\nEdge: p2 month plan: start -2 end +28; checkins in range: c1,c2 → 175; target 25h=1500min → 12% → progress 12.\\n\\nOK write harness3 now. Keep it robust: wrap each test in try/catch, collect failures, exit code.\\n\\nAlso note: mount handlers use `App.store.subscribe` — my stub returns noop unsubscribe — fine.\\n\\nOne more: OVERVIEW mount calls setRoll → needs el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-roll[data-target]\') → jsdom works; setRoll uses element.firstChild etc. — real DOM, fine. el.classList.add(\'st-roll-noanim\') fine. `void el.offsetWidth` fine.\\n\\nAlso overview unmount: document.getElementById(\'content\') — el._unsub exists (noop) → calls it. fine.\\n\\nWriting now.\",\"content\":\"jsdom 可用性检查被预检拦截，我将它并入 act 测试。先编写基于 jsdom 的 mount 交互级测试。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"jsdom 可用性检查被预检拦截，我将它并入 act 测试。先编写基于 jsdom 的 mount 交互级测试。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":27,\"round\":27,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":27,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:49:32'),
