(1166, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 152718, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'skeleton', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"skeleton-turn-28\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Key compatibility facts confirmed:\\n\\n1. study.js `pathSegs(k)` uses `split(/\\\\s*>\\\\s*/)` — my seed knowledge paths use \'行测 > 言语理解 > 逻辑填空\' (spaces around >) — matches perfectly ✓\\n2. MASTERY_NAMES[m-1] — my mastery values 1-3 fit ✓\\n3. study.js uses `App.store.settings.studyUI` / `studyClock` via updateSettings — my updateSettings shallow-merges arbitrary keys ✓\\n4. work.js registers \'/work\' ✓ — so earlier 404 for \'/work\' was mid-write. Need to re-test.\\n5. They use template literals and modern JS — fine.\\n\\nOne thing I noticed: study.js line 27 `if (!App || !App.store) return;` — they check `App` bare (global). Fine.\\n\\nNow, let me also check whether the parallel tasks modified store.js (my settings getter fix intact) or CSS. store.js LastWriteTime 21:36:57 — that was my edit time (21:36). Actually my edit happened around then; the earlier smoke test found the bug and I fixed at ~21:35-36. So store.js is mine. But wait — do the parallel page files depend on store fields my seed lacks? E.g., work.js uses `todos.update(id, {done, completedAt})` — completedAt is just an extra field, fine.\\n\\nAlso — did parallel tasks perhaps expect `App.store.settings` to include extra defaults? They use studyUI/studyClock lazily with `|| {}`. Fine.\\n\\nNow re-run full verification with the final files (work.js may still be being written by the parallel task — it was 21:38, and it\'s now later; risk of mid-write changes but nothing I can do; I\'ll just re-test). Also re-verify store.js getter fix is intact and node --check passes for all files again (work/study are now parallel-owned; check their syntax too since they load in the page).\\n\\nThen run the full E2E interaction test (sidebar toggle, topbar search/settings, theme, font, 404, clear data flow) using a temp copy of index.html.\\n\\nNote: I must be careful — the E2E test harness loads current work.js/study.js which register many pages; my test navigates to /work etc. The tests I planned use /settings, /search, /home, unregistered path — all fine regardless of work/study state.\\n\\nAlso for the clear-data test: after clearAll, todos.count()===6 ✓ (seed has 6 todos; parallel tasks didn\'t change seeds since store.js is mine... unless they did. Let me verify store.js still has 6 seed todos — check quickly with grep count of \'seed-todo-\'.\\n\\nLet me first re-run node --check on all JS (including the now-large work.js/study.js) and verify store.js content integrity, then browser tests.\",\"content\":\"study.js 的 pathSegs 使用 `split(/\\\\s*>\\\\s*/)`，与我的种子路径「行测 > 言语理解 > 逻辑填空」完全匹配；mastery 1-3 也兼容。现在复检所有 JS 语法（含并行模块）+ store.js 完整性：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"study.js 的 pathSegs 使用 `split(/\\\\s*>\\\\s*/)`，与我的种子路径「行测 > 言语理解 > 逻辑填空」完全匹配；mastery 1-3 也兼容。现在复检所有 JS 语法（含并行模块）+ store.js 完整性：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":28,\"round\":28,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":28,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:50:34'),
