(1200, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 154380, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'skeleton', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"skeleton-turn-30\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"27/29 pass. The 2 failures: 侧边栏折叠/展开 — `sb.classList.contains(\'collapsed\')` false after clicking #sidebar-toggle.\\n\\nWhy? The toggle handler:\\n```js\\nvar toggle = sidebar.querySelector(\'#sidebar-toggle\');\\nif (toggle) {\\n  toggle.addEventListener(\'click\', function () {\\n    var collapsed = sidebar.classList.toggle(\'collapsed\');\\n    App.store.updateSettings({ sidebarCollapsed: collapsed });\\n  });\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis looks correct. But wait — maybe the click on the toggle button... The toggle button is inside `.sidebar-head`. Is there another click handler that interferes? The sidebar has a delegated click listener:\\n\\n```js\\nsidebar.addEventListener(\'click\', function (e) {\\n  var nav = e.target.closest(\'[data-path]\');\\n  if (nav) { e.preventDefault(); App.navigate(nav.dataset.path); return; }\\n  var t = e.target.closest(\'[data-toggle-group]\');\\n  ...\\n});\\n```\\n\\nThe toggle button has no data-path, so no interference. Hmm.\\n\\nWait — maybe the problem is the click doesn\'t fire because... the toggle button is `#sidebar-toggle`. In the E2E test, `st.click()` — programmatic click on a button element. Should fire the listener.\\n\\nUnless... initSidebar is never called! Let me check boot: boot() calls initSidebar(). boot runs on DOMContentLoaded. In the E2E harness, the test script ALSO registers a DOMContentLoaded listener... wait, no — the test script uses `(async function(){...})()` immediately, not waiting for DOMContentLoaded! The test script is at the end of body; it runs DURING parsing, BEFORE DOMContentLoaded fires. So at test start, boot() hasn\'t run yet — initSidebar not called → toggle has no listener → click does nothing → classList unchanged → FAIL.\\n\\nBut then how did other tests pass? Theme buttons etc. work because... hmm, those are in /settings which requires boot to have run (registerPage etc.). Wait — App.navigate(\'/search\') worked (hash changed). But navigate is App.navigate — which works regardless of boot (router.navigate works without contentEl). The search page rendered because... hashchange listener was registered at router.js load; navigate sets location.hash → hashchange fires → render() runs (contentEl null though!). Hmm, but the test found `#search-input` rendered...\\n\\nWait — actually the async test runs with awaits: `st.click(); await wait(260);` — the first await yields to the event loop. DOMContentLoaded fires during that await (parsing finishes quickly). Then boot runs (registered listener fires), initSidebar binds listeners. But the FIRST click on toggle already happened BEFORE boot → no listener → FAIL #1. Then second click after another 260ms — by then boot has run and listener is bound... but the first click didn\'t toggle, so the second click toggles ONCE (adds collapsed) → `!sb.classList.contains(\'collapsed\')` is false → FAIL #2.\\n\\nThat explains exactly the two failures — a test timing artifact, not an app bug. The app works: user clicks happen after load.\\n\\nTo confirm, I should re-run the E2E with the test starting after DOMContentLoaded. Let me fix the test to wait for DOMContentLoaded first.\\n\\nAlso note: virtual-time-budget with setTimeout — fine.\\n\\nLet me rerun with the test wrapped in DOMContentLoaded (or simply start after `await wait(50)` — but cleanest: listen for DOMContentLoaded).\",\"content\":\"27/29 通过。2 个失败是**测试时序问题**：测试脚本在 DOMContentLoaded 之前运行，boot() 尚未绑定折叠按钮监听器。修正测试脚本等待 DOMContentLoaded 后重跑：\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"27/29 通过。2 个失败是**测试时序问题**：测试脚本在 DOMContentLoaded 之前运行，boot() 尚未绑定折叠按钮监听器。修正测试脚本等待 DOMContentLoaded 后重跑：\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":30,\"round\":30,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":30,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 13:57:18'),
