(1343, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 172524, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-41\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Static cross-check passes: 47 rendered ids, 61 selector references all resolvable.\\n\\nNow let me do a final careful code review pass of key sections to catch logic issues that tests can\'t (mount interactions). Let me re-read the file\'s critical parts, especially:\\n1. OVERVIEW_DEF.mount — the subscribe handler references `r.getAttribute(\'data-roll-key\')` but I never set data-roll-key in render! Let me check: in render, stat cards have `<span class=\\\"st-roll\\\" data-target=\\\"${...}\\\" data-val=\\\"0\\\">`. The subscribe callback does `var key = r.getAttribute(\'data-roll-key\')` → null → v = null → setRoll(el, null) → target 0! That would reset numbers to 0 on every store change. BUG. I need to fix: either set data-roll-key in render or key the update differently.\\n\\nLooking at my render code: the three rolls are 本周时长 (target = weekMin/60), 连续天数 (streak), 计划完成率 (rate). I didn\'t add data-roll-key attributes. The subscribe handler keys off data-roll-key → all get null → setRoll(el, 0)?? Let me fix by adding data-roll-key attributes in render and mapping in subscribe.\\n\\nFix:\\n- render: `<span class=\\\"st-roll\\\" data-roll-key=\\\"week\\\" data-target=\\\"...\\\">`, `<span class=\\\"st-roll\\\" data-roll-key=\\\"streak\\\" ...>`, `<span class=\\\"st-roll\\\" data-roll-key=\\\"rate\\\" ...>`.\\n- subscribe: key===\'week\' → weekMin hours; \'streak\' → s.streak; \'rate\' → s.rate; default → keep target attr? For robustness: v = computed or r.getAttribute(\'data-target\').\\n\\n2. TREE_DEF mount subscribe: refreshList called on any store change — fine.\\n\\n3. In OVERVIEW mount, initial roll: `setRoll(r, r.getAttribute(\'data-target\'))` — data-target=\\\"12\\\" etc. For weekMin decimal e.g. 4.5 → Math.round(4.5)=5? Hmm! setRoll rounds: `Math.round(Number(value)||0)`. data-target for week is `${Math.round(s.weekMin/60*10)/10}` e.g. \\\"4.5\\\" → setRoll rounds to 5? That breaks the decimal display: the roll shows \\\"5\\\" but the unit is 小时 and sub shows 共 270 分钟. The value 4.5h rounded to 5 is misleading.\\n\\nBetter: keep the decimal display as static text (not rolled), OR roll only integer part. Simplest: for the week stat, show static value (e.g. \\\"4.5\\\") without roll; roll only streak & rate (integers). The requirement: \\\"数字从 store 实时读取，数值变化带微小数字滚动动画\\\" — applies to the numbers; streak and rate rolling satisfies it. For duration, static is fine. But my current code applies setRoll to the week span too → rounds 4.5→5 (initial roll sets data-val to \\\"5\\\" — wait, initial: data-val=\\\"0\\\", data-target=\\\"4.5\\\". mount: setRoll(el, \\\"4.5\\\") → target=Math.round(4.5)=5? Math.round(4.5)=5 (rounds half up). So displays 5. That\'s wrong.\\n\\nFix options:\\na) Don\'t roll the decimal; render week duration as plain text `<span class=\\\"st-stat-num\\\">4.5</span>`.\\nb) Make setRoll support decimals: roll digit-by-digit including \'.\'? Complex.\\n\\nI\'ll go with (a): week stat num is static text; streak & rate rolls. But then \\\"数值变化带微小数字滚动动画\\\" still satisfied by streak/rate/cards? The entry card summaries are text with numbers — I said they\'d have roll spans but I actually didn\'t add roll spans to entry summaries (sum strings like \'已收录 5 个知识点\' plain text). Hmm, the requirement is about 数据卡数字 rolling. Stat cards: streak (integer roll ✓), rate (integer roll ✓), week duration (static ✗). \\n\\nAlternative better: make week duration roll with integer part AND decimal handled as text? Overkill. Let me instead roll \\\"分钟\\\" integer? The stat shows 小时 with 1 decimal — I could display hours rounded to integer for the roll and keep detail in sub? That loses precision.\\n\\nCleaner: roll the streak and rate; for week hours, show static \\\"4.5\\\". Actually, I can still animate: count-up effect without digit roll — e.g., animate the number with a small scale pulse on change. Simplest robust: keep static.\\n\\nDecision:\\n- week stat: `<span class=\\\"st-stat-num\\\" id=\\\"st-stat-week\\\">4.5</span><span class=\\\"st-stat-unit\\\">小时</span>` static text updated on subscribe (textContent).\\n- streak/rate: roll spans with data-roll-key.\\n\\nImplement:\\nrender:\\n```\\n<div class=\\\"st-stat-num\\\"><span id=\\\"st-stat-week\\\">${(s.weekMin/60).toFixed(1)}</span><span class=\\\"st-stat-unit\\\">小时</span></div>\\n...\\n<div class=\\\"st-stat-num\\\"><span class=\\\"st-roll\\\" data-roll-key=\\\"streak\\\" data-target=\\\"${s.streak}\\\" data-val=\\\"0\\\">0</span><span class=\\\"st-stat-unit\\\">天</span></div>\\n<div class=\\\"st-stat-num\\\"><span class=\\\"st-roll\\\" data-roll-key=\\\"rate\\\" data-target=\\\"${s.rate}\\\" data-val=\\\"0\\\">0</span><span class=\\\"st-stat-unit\\\">%</span></div>\\n```\\nmount:\\n```\\nel.querySelectorAll(\'.st-roll[data-roll-key]\').forEach(function(r){ setRoll(r, r.getAttribute(\'data-target\')); });\\nvar weekEl = el.querySelector(\'#st-stat-week\');\\nsubscribe: \\n  s = overviewStats();\\n  if (weekEl) weekEl.textContent = (s.weekMin/60).toFixed(1);\\n  el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-roll[data-roll-key]\').forEach(function(r){\\n    var key=r.getAttribute(\'data-roll-key\');\\n    var v = key===\'streak\'? s.streak : s.rate;\\n    setRoll(r, v);\\n  });\\n```\\nAlso the sub texts (共 X 分钟 / N 个进行中计划) — update on subscribe too? They\'re static in render; update for correctness: give ids. I\'ll update week sub and rate sub too. Minor. I\'ll add ids: st-stat-week-sub, st-stat-rate-sub and update.\\n\\nAlso entry cards summaries are static; on subscribe the numbers there stale. Given overview is rarely the active page during store changes, acceptable — but easy to update: skip (scope). Actually let me also refresh entry summaries via ids to be thorough? That\'s 6 more ids. Hmm. The subscribe path mostly matters when other pages mutate store while overview mounted — impossible (single page view). So minimal updates suffice. I\'ll just fix the week display & roll keys.\\n\\n4. `clockElapsed` cross-day clamp: `ms += Math.max(0, dayStart.getTime() - st.startedAt)` — if startedAt is before dayStart, adds dayStart-startedAt — correct (accumulated includes only up to midnight).\\n\\n5. CLOCK_DEF submit: reads `st` local var — after mount, st is local copy; chips toggle updates st.modules and persists. submit uses st — ok. But note: if user paused and reloaded page, new mount reads persisted state — fine.\\n\\n6. WRONG_DEF: `renderReview` for queue exhaustion shows done panel; `data-review-exit` buttons bound in renderReview — also the done panel has `[data-review-exit]` but binding happens... in renderReview, after setting innerHTML, we query `reviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'[data-review-exit]\')` — done panel includes that button ✓.\\n\\nWait — in renderReview, when queue exhausted, we return early AFTER setting innerHTML — but binding of `[data-review-exit]` happens after the early return? Let me check my code:\\n\\n```js\\nfunction renderReview() {\\n  var w = reviewQueue[reviewIdx];\\n  if (!w) {\\n    reviewBox.innerHTML = `...<button data-review-exit>返回错题本</button>`;\\n    return;   // ← early return, no binding!\\n  }\\n  ...\\n  reviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'[data-review-exit]\').forEach(...)\\n}\\n```\\nBUG: the done panel\'s exit button never gets its click handler. Fix: bind before early return, or restructure:\\n\\n```js\\nif (!w) { reviewBox.innerHTML = doneHtml; bindExit(); return; }\\n```\\nI\'ll add binding: after setting done innerHTML, `var ex = reviewBox.querySelector(\'[data-review-exit]\'); if (ex) ex.addEventListener(\'click\', exitReview);` before return.\\n\\n7. `submitReview` — after result, next button handler: `reviewIdx++; reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'; renderReview();` ✓.\\n\\n8. enterReview when queue empty (id not found) → toast \'该题无需复习\'? enterReview: `if (reviewIdx < 0) { toast; return; }` — but w.status!==\'archived\' check filters queue; clicking a pending/learning item → found. OK.\\n\\n9. In `renderReview` missing-question branch: removes the wrong record and increments reviewIdx then renderReview — recursion fine.\\n\\n10. QUESTIONS_DEF mount: `focusId` handling — after renderList, if focusId set, we clear it inside renderList (focusId=\'\'). But renderList is called again on filter changes... focusId already \'\'. OK. However there\'s a subtle bug: `var focusId = pendingFocus; pendingFocus=\'\';` at mount — then renderList uses focusId. Fine.\\n\\n11. Questions answer reveal: `maskEl.classList.remove(\'st-answer-mask\')` — the class provides blur. Then textContent replaced with answer (unblurred since class removed) ✓. But we also removed mask class from a span that was inline-block; fine.\\n\\n12. Question card toggle: clicking the card body toggles (unless button). The answer button click also bubbles to card click → toggles card! `listBox.addEventListener(\'click\', ...)` handler: first checks `e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')` → handles answer → `return;` — so no card toggle. Good. But the toggle button is inside .st-q-extra; clicking it → data-action toggle → handled, return ✓.\\n\\nHowever: clicking \\\"标记为错题\\\"/\\\"删除\\\" buttons → handled, return ✓.\\n\\n13. In wrong page, `itemHTML` — `w.lastResult === true ? \'✅\' : w.lastResult === false && w.reviewCount ? \'❌\' : \'—\'` ✓.\\n\\n14. PLAN_DEF.mount: `renderChart(el.querySelector(\'#st-plan-chart\'), view)` — renderChart sets innerHTML with bars; rAF then sets heights via data-h ✓. Also target line uses `bottom: X%` — the .st-target-line is positioned absolute inside .st-chart (position:relative) ✓.\\n\\n15. Plan card detail: `.st-plan-detail` hidden toggle ✓.\\n\\n16. openNewPlanModal: type buttons binding inside onConfirm — the seg-btn click listeners are added INSIDE onConfirm (after open). Since modal is open, user can click buttons before confirming — listeners added at confirm time, so type clicks before confirm are lost... Actually onConfirm is invoked when user clicks 确认. The seg buttons are in the modal; user clicks 月计划 then 确认 → onConfirm runs → binds listeners (too late!) → type stays \'week\'. BUG. Fix: bind type buttons immediately after openModal (outside onConfirm), like mastery modal does.\\n\\nRestructure openNewPlanModal:\\n```js\\nvar type = \'week\';\\nvar mask = App.openModal(html, { onConfirm: ... uses type });\\nvar seg = mask.querySelector(\'#np-type\');\\nseg.querySelectorAll(\'.seg-btn\').forEach(function(b){ b.addEventListener(\'click\', function(){ type = b.dataset.type; seg.querySelectorAll(\'.seg-btn\').forEach(function(x){x.classList.toggle(\'active\', x===b);}); }); });\\n```\\nRemove the binding from onConfirm.\\n\\n17. openAddQuestionModal / openImportModal / openAddShizhengModal / openWrongModal — read inputs at confirm time (fine, no pre-binding needed). openWrongModal reason radios — checked read at confirm ✓.\\n\\n18. DETAIL_DEF.mount mastery modal: binding after openModal ✓ (outside onConfirm). But there\'s a subtlety: `mask.querySelectorAll(\'.st-mastery-opt\')` — mask returned by App.openModal ✓.\\n\\n19. DETAIL_DEF.mount: `var id = el.querySelector(\'#st-mastery-pill\') ? ... : detailIdFromPath(location.hash);` — pill exists normally → id from dataset ✓.\\n\\n20. Reading mode: exitReading referenced in unmount via el._exitReading ✓; onKey removed ✓.\\n\\n21. TREE_DEF: `data-select` key split(\'/\') — selected stored as array; `ts.selected.join(\'/\')` used in treeHTML selectedKey compare ✓.\\n\\n22. treeState default expanded: `{\'行测\': true, \'行测/判断推理\': true}` — note actual key for 判断推理 node is \'行测/判断推理\' ✓ (segs.concat). And arrow toggles key \'行测\' etc ✓.\\n\\n23. Overview subscribe handler — fix needed (see #1).\\n\\n24. CLOCK_DEF: on submit, if modules empty, checkin.modules = [] — fine.\\n\\n25. `streakDays` used in clock render ✓.\\n\\n26. Shizheng mount: month label update — rerender via App.refresh() — in real app, refresh re-renders the whole page (render+mount) ✓. In my design rerender() = App.refresh(). OK.\\n\\nBut wait — shizheng\'s setYM: `setUI({szMonth: v, szTag: tag})` then rerender — App.refresh() calls router.render() which re-renders current path with fresh getUI ✓.\\n\\n27. One more: PLAN_DEF render calls planCardHTML for active plans — planCardHTML uses moduleActual which reads checkins — fine.\\n\\n28. renderChart label uses `esc(v.label.replace(\'\\\\n\', \'<br>\'))` — wait, `esc()` escapes the \'<br>\' → \'<br>\' becomes \'&lt;br&gt;\' — displayed literally as <br> text! BUG. In week view label = \'周一\\\\n8月3日\'? Let me check: `units.push({ label: names[i] + \'\\\\n\' + fmtMD(ds) ...})` — label contains \'\\\\n\'. In template: `<span class=\\\"st-chart-x\\\">${esc(v.label.replace(\'\\\\n\', \'<br>\'))}</span>` — esc converts \'<\' → \'&lt;\' so <br> shows as literal text. Need to escape parts separately: `esc(name) + \'<br>\' + esc(date)`. Fix: store label as {name, date} or split. Simplest: change label to array or precompute two fields. I\'ll modify: units.push({label: names[i], sub: fmtMD(ds), ...}) and render `<span class=\\\"st-chart-x\\\">${esc(v.label)}<br>${esc(v.sub)}</span>`. For month: label \'第N周\', sub \'\'.\\n\\n29. `fmtDue` for nextReview of wrong: overdue shows \'已逾期 N 天\' as plain text (not tag) — in itemHTML overdue span gets class tag tag-danger ✓.\\n\\n30. setRoll initial in overview mount: `setRoll(r, r.getAttribute(\'data-target\'))` — with data-target \\\"5\\\" → rolls 0→5 ✓.\\n\\n31. `clockElapsed` in CLOCK_DEF mount initial st clamp — after clamp we `saveClockState(st)` — ok.\\n\\n32. Overview `_unsub` stored on el; unmount reads document.getElementById(\'content\')._unsub — matches.\\n\\n33. In OVERVIEW_DEF.mount subscribe — also needs updating entry summaries? Skipping (documented above).\\n\\n34. CLOCK_DEF.mount: `resetBtn.disabled = !st.running && elapsed === 0;` — after start & pause, elapsed>0 → enabled ✓. But refresh() is called every 500ms; if running, resetBtn disabled? `!st.running` false → disabled=false ✓ (reset enabled while running — ok).\\n\\n35. QUESTIONS filter select options: modules list built from ALL_MODULES intersected with existing question modules; if questions exist with module \'未分类\' etc. Hmm — module select default \'全部模块\'; if a question has module not in list, can\'t filter by it but still visible under 全部. Fine.\\n\\nAlso — search-box wrapper for #st-q-search uses .search-box .input padding-left 38px + inline style — ok.\\n\\n36. `openQuestion` from detail — navigates to \'/study/questions\' ✓; QUESTIONS mount reads pendingFocus ✓. But if user is already on \'/study/questions\' and clicks related question? Not possible (detail page separate).\\n\\n37. Wrong page archived click → toast \'已归档\' ✓.\\n\\n38. In `renderReview` step, `reviewBox.dataset.locked` — dataset on div ✓.\\n\\n39. `submitReview` sets `reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'1\'` in option click handler before calling submitReview — yes inside click handler: `reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'1\'` then submitReview. ✓ prevents double submit.\\n\\n40. PLAN_DEF render: history section — done plans. Auto-complete happens in mount (not render) — initial direct-hash load: render shows active; mount processes completion → but render already done; App.refresh not called after mount processing. So a plan that expired today shows stale until next interaction. Minor: after processing in mount, if any changes were made, call App.refresh()? That would re-render once. Let me add: track changed flag; if changed, rerender. Careful about infinite loop: after refresh, mount runs again, recomputes — progress already stored (same value) → no update → no refresh. OK safe. I\'ll add.\\n\\n41. Chart: `esc(v.label.replace(\'\\\\n\',\'<br>\'))` fix (see #28).\\n\\n42. `st-chart-bar.ghost` — border dashed ✓.\\n\\n43. `renderChart` target line bottom % — bottom: targetPct% from bottom where bars grow from bottom — consistent ✓.\\n\\n44. In PLAN_DEF.mount, `el.querySelector(\'#st-plan-seg\')` click → setUI + rerender ✓.\\n\\n45. openNewPlanModal title uses isoWeek ✓.\\n\\n46. One more potential issue: OVERVIEW render — entries use data-nav=\\\"/study/plan\\\" (task path) ✓ registered. \\n\\n47. In `TREE_DEF.mount` — `listBox.addEventListener(\'click\')` for `[data-open]` — openKnowledge ✓.\\n\\n48. `ensureKnowledgeRoutes` at load — called once; new knowledge added via import later → openKnowledge registers exact path before navigate ✓.\\n\\n49. CLOCK_DEF: `chipsBox.querySelectorAll(\'.st-module-chip\')` — render has them ✓.\\n\\n50. In `DETAIL_DEF.render`, `k.commonPoints || [...]` — seed has none → defaults ✓.\\n\\nAlso #27 in harness: no.\\n\\nNow also double-check the template in render for plan chart: `box.innerHTML = \\\\`${targetPct>0?...}\\\\` + values.map...` — I wrote:\\n```\\nbox.innerHTML = `\\n  ${targetPct > 0 ? \'<div class=\\\"st-target-line\\\" ...\' : \'\'}\\n  ${values.map(...).join(\'\')}`;\\n```\\n✓.\\n\\nAnd in the bar col: `title=\\\"${fmtHM(v.actual)}\\\"` — fmtHM(0) = \'0分钟\' ok.\\n\\nGhost bar data-h: `Math.max(2, targetPct)`.\\n\\nOne more: `.st-chart` height 178px with padding-top 14px; bars area flex:1 ✓.\\n\\nNow implement fixes:\\nA. Overview: week stat static + roll keys + subscribe fix.\\nB. Wrong done-panel exit binding.\\nC. Plan modal type binding outside onConfirm.\\nD. Chart label <br> escaping.\\nE. Plan mount: refresh if auto-changed.\\n\\nLet me apply these edits now.\",\"content\":\"静态校验通过，但我在复查中发现了 5 处需要修复的逻辑问题（测试桩覆盖不到的交互细节）：\\n1. 总览页 subscribe 回调读取 `data-roll-key` 但 render 未设置该属性 → 数据变更时数字会被错误归零；且小数时长会被 `Math.round` 破坏；\\n2. 错题复习完成面板的「返回错题本」按钮未绑定事件（early return）；\\n3. 新建计划弹窗的类型切换监听绑定在 onConfirm 内部 → 用户点击类型后再确认时监听尚未挂上，类型永远为 week；\\n4. 柱状图标签 `esc()` 会转义 `<br>`，换行会显示为字面量；\\n5. 计划到期自动完成后未刷新界面。\\n\\n逐一修复。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"静态校验通过，但我在复查中发现了 5 处需要修复的逻辑问题（测试桩覆盖不到的交互细节）： 1. 总览页 subscribe 回调读取 `data-roll-key` 但 render 未设置该属性 → 数据变更时数字会被错误归零；且小数时长会被 `Math.round` 破坏； 2. 错题复习完成面板的「返回错题本」按钮未绑定事件（early return）； 3. 新建计划弹窗的类型切换监听绑定在 onConfirm 内部 → 用户点击类型后再确认时监听尚未挂上，类型永远为…\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":41,\"round\":41,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":41,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 14:15:47'),
(1344, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 172525, 'tool.started', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_work', 'call_00_2VtxXtchLHvQXp3Jw8XY0201', '{\"tool_key\":\"python_executor\",\"display_name\":\"Python 执行器\",\"arguments\":{\"code\":\"import subprocess, os\\n\\nchrome = r\'C:\\\\Program Files\\\\Google\\\\Chrome\\\\Application\\\\chrome.exe\'\\nbase = \'file:///D:/Project/Project/ccee/web1/index.html\'\\n\\nchecks = [\\n    (\'#/work\', [\'work-overview\', \'我的工作区\', \'今日待办\', \'收件箱\', \'项目备忘\', \'会议与日志\']),\\n    (\'#/work/todos\', [\'work-todos\', \'重要紧急\', \'重要不紧急\', \'紧急不重要\', \'不重要不紧急\', \'新建待办\', \'快速添加待办\']),\\n    (\'#/work/inbox\', [\'work-inbox\', \'未清理\', \'一键清空已完成\', \'记一下\']),\\n    (\'#/work/projects\', [\'work-projects\', \'新建项目\', \'产品 3.0 改版\', \'公考行测刷题计划\', \'搜索项目名\']),\\n    (\'#/work/projects/seed-proj-1\', [\'work-detail\', \'产品 3.0 改版\', \'创建日期\', \'任务\', \'笔记\', \'文件\', \'添加任务\']),\\n    (\'#/work/log\', [\'work-log\', \'生成周报\', \'生成月报\', \'完成时间线\']),\\n    (\'#/work/meetings\', [\'work-meetings\', \'新建会议记录\', \'项目周会\', \'需求评审会\']),\\n    (\'#/work/logs\', [\'work-log\', \'生成周报\']),  # 侧边栏复数路径别名\\n]\\n\\nuser_data = os.path.join(os.environ.get(\'TEMP\', \'.\'), \'wb_chrome_profile2\')\\nos.makedirs(user_data, exist_ok=True)\\n\\nresults = []\\nfor frag, keywords in checks:\\n    url = base + frag\\n    try:\\n        r = subprocess.run([\\n            chrome, \'--headless=new\', \'--disable-gpu\', \'--no-sandbox\',\\n            \'--user-data-dir=\' + user_data,\\n            \'--virtual-time-budget=4000\', \'--dump-dom\', url\\n        ], capture_output=True, timeout=60)\\n        dom = r.stdout.decode(\'utf-8\', errors=\'replace\')\\n        missing = [k for k in keywords if k not in dom]\\n        results.append((frag, r.returncode, missing, len(dom)))\\n    except Exception as e:\\n        results.append((frag, -1, [str(e)], 0))\\n\\nprint(\'=== 端到端渲染验证 v2（Chrome headless --dump-dom） ===\')\\nallok = True\\nfor frag, rc, missing, domlen in results:\\n    ok = rc == 0 and not missing\\n    if not ok:\\n        allok = False\\n    print((\'PASS\' if ok else \'FAIL\'), frag, \'| exit=\', rc, \'| domlen=\', domlen, \'| missing=\', missing)\\nprint(\'\\\\nALL PASS\' if allok else \'\\\\nHAS FAILURES\')\\n\"},\"effect\":\"write\",\"risk_level\":\"high\",\"phase\":null,\"operation_id\":null,\"intent\":null,\"shell\":null,\"command_fingerprint\":null}', '2026-08-03 14:15:47'),
