(1415, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 176590, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-50\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"All 5 fixes applied. Wait — there\'s a subtlety with fix 5: `if (changed) { App.refresh(); return; }` — `return` inside mount callback returns from mount — fine. But `App.refresh()` triggers render → mount again — the new mount recomputes (no changes) → proceeds to bind events. OK.\\n\\nBut hmm — there\'s an issue: my harness test for plan asserted progress update. With the `changed → refresh → return` path, mount returns early after refresh; the harness stubs refresh as noop → mount returns without binding events → later clicks on plan page in harness3 would fail. But harness3 is currently skipped (no jsdom). harness2 only tests render. OK.\\n\\nAnother check on fix 1: `setRoll(r, r.getAttribute(\'data-target\'))` — for streak/rate ints ✓.\\n\\nNow re-run the full test suite: syntax check + harness + harness2 + harness4.\",\"content\":\"5 处修复完成。重新运行全部校验（语法 + 加载 + 渲染冒烟 + 静态交叉）。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"5 处修复完成。重新运行全部校验（语法 + 加载 + 渲染冒烟 + 静态交叉）。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":50,\"round\":50,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":50,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 14:25:28'),
