(1422, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 177498, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-51\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"All four checks pass. Now, since jsdom isn\'t reliably available, let me write a minimal-but-functional DOM shim test to exercise mount-level interactions for the most critical flows. Actually — I reconsidered: writing a mini-DOM is error-prone and may produce false confidence. \\n\\nAlternative: There IS one more possibility for jsdom — maybe the sandbox\'s npm install went into the executor\'s isolated overlay, and `node` inside the SAME shell call can see it. My earlier `node -e require(...)` was a separate call — maybe the FS differs per call? The install call and the require call were different invocations. But the study-jsdom dir was empty on disk from a different call too... The sandbox likely gives each invocation a fresh overlay — no persistence across calls. That explains everything: mkdir created dir in overlay → real FS shows empty; npm install created node_modules in overlay → subsequent call can\'t see it.\\n\\nConclusion: no jsdom within one call — unless install AND test run in the SAME shell invocation! I can do: `cd tempdir && npm install jsdom --silent && node harness3.js` in one command — the overlay persists within one call? The install output said \\\"added 38 packages, and removed 9 packages in 1m\\\" — took 1 minute. If within one call the overlay persists, then install+test in one command works. Worth one try: `cd /d %TEMP%\\\\study-jsdom && npm install jsdom --no-audit --no-fund --loglevel=error && node C:\\\\...\\\\study-harness3.js` — but harness3 requires jsdom from the absolute path `C:/Users/.../Temp/study-jsdom/node_modules/jsdom`. Within the same overlay, that path would exist. Also harness3 requires study.js from D:\\\\ — real FS, fine.\\n\\nBut if the overlay doesn\'t persist even within a call (i.e., install writes to real disk but my earlier check was on a different... hmm, actually the dir existed on real disk but empty — so mkdir DID write to real disk. Then npm install — where did 38 packages go? If cd /d worked, node_modules should be in study-jsdom on real disk... unless npm used a cache + symlink layout? \\\"removed 9 packages\\\" implies it operated on an existing node_modules somewhere. Maybe npm walked UP from study-jsdom and found C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\node_modules? I searched Temp for jsdom* dirs — nothing. Hmm, maybe it found node_modules in %APPDATA%\\\\npm (global) and installed there? Global root listing showed only pptxgenjs & prettier — no jsdom.\\n\\nActually wait — \\\"removed 9 packages\\\" — if npm treated the project as already having a node_modules (from a previous npm state in overlay?), or npm ci cache... Whatever. One more attempt within a single call, but with --prefix to force location:\\n\\n`npm install --prefix C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\study-jsdom jsdom --no-audit --no-fund --loglevel=error && node C:\\\\...\\\\study-harness3.js`\\n\\n--prefix forces install location. If this works and harness3 passes, great. Time cost ~1min. Let me try once — blocking=false finite.\\n\\nIf it fails again, I\'ll accept the current validation level (syntax + load + render + static) and do a final manual review of mount code. Actually, you know what — let me also consider: maybe I can make harness3 not need jsdom at all by writing a compact DOM emulation focused on what my pages use: innerHTML parsing is the hard part (querySelector on parsed HTML). Without a parser, emulating is very hard.\\n\\nLet me try the --prefix one-shot.\",\"content\":\"4 项校验全部通过。沙箱的文件系统似乎是按调用隔离的（npm 安装结果跨调用不可见）。做最后一次尝试：安装与测试放同一次调用内（`--prefix` 强制路径）。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"4 项校验全部通过。沙箱的文件系统似乎是按调用隔离的（npm 安装结果跨调用不可见）。做最后一次尝试：安装与测试放同一次调用内（`--prefix` 强制路径）。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration