(1471, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 199908, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-59\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Great progress! Now the remaining failures are much fewer and more specific. Analyze:\\n\\n1. **`overview: 数字未滚动到目标值, val=2`** — Expected streak=1 (harness checkins: c1 today, c2 -1 → streak should be 2! c1 today (55min>0), c2 yesterday (120min>0) → streak = 2. My test asserted `!== String(1)` — WRONG EXPECTATION, should be 2. Test bug. Fix: assert === \'2\'.\\n\\n2. **`questions: 卡片展开失败`** — still failing! And `questions: 错题原因弹窗缺失, html=<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">...` — interesting! The modalState.html DOES contain the wrong-reason modal (\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\" with radios — that\'s openWrongModal\'s html!). But my test checks `modalState.html.indexOf(\'粗心\') < 0` — the html shows `<label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` and... wait the check failed meaning \'粗心\' not found?? The html shown starts with `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` — hmm, this is the mastery modal? No — mastery modal has `st-mastery-opt` too (detail page). The openWrongModal html: `<p class=\\\"st-form-hint\\\">这道题当时为什么错了？...` + REASON_TAGS labels with `<span class=\\\"tag tag-warn\\\">粗心</span>`. The snippet shows `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` — openWrongModal uses st-mastery-opt labels ✓ and inside should have `<span class=\\\"tag tag-warn\\\">粗心</span>`. The snippet truncated at 60 chars — can\'t see. Hmm, but `indexOf(\'粗心\')` — the html DOES contain \'粗心\' as radio value: `value=\\\"粗心\\\"` — hmm value attribute in html: `<input type=\\\"radio\\\" name=\\\"wrong-reason\\\" value=\\\"粗心\\\" checked>` — indexOf(\'粗心\') should find it!\\n\\nWAIT — look at the order of test steps: click q1 toggle → expand fail; click answer → mask check... then `click q2 toggle`, `click wrong` → openWrongModal → html has 粗心... but the failure message shows html starting `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` — that\'s the WRONG-REASON modal (which uses st-mastery-opt labels). So modal DID open with correct html, but \'粗心\' not found?? The radio value attribute... in jsdom innerHTML parse: `<input ... value=\\\"粗心\\\">` — attribute present. indexOf on the html STRING — \'粗心\' should literally be in the string.\\n\\nUnless... the failure happened on an EARLIER check: my test does click q1 toggle FIRST → \'questions: 卡片展开失败\' pushed (no exception). Then answer → no failure. Then q2 toggle + wrong → openWrongModal... but modalState.html may have been OVERWRITTEN by a later modal? No — the wrong-click check is the next assertion.\\n\\nHmm wait — actually, let me re-read the test sequence:\\n\\n```js\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');\\nvar card1 = ...;\\nif (!card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')) failures.push(\'questions: 卡片展开失败\');\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] [data-action=\\\"answer\\\"]\');\\nif (card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\')) failures.push(\'questions: 答案遮罩未移除\');\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q2\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q2\\\"] [data-action=\\\"wrong\\\"]\');\\nif (modalState.html.indexOf(\'粗心\') < 0) failures.push(\'questions: 错题原因弹窗缺失, html=\' + modalState.html.slice(0, 60));\\n```\\n\\nThe html snippet: `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` — so openWrongModal RAN (modalState.html set). \'粗心\' — the first reason option is \'粗心\' — the html should contain it... UNLESS escapeHtml? No, reasons are static strings, not escaped. Hmm — `REASON_TAGS.map` — options html: `<label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt...\\\"><input type=\\\"radio\\\" name=\\\"wrong-reason\\\" value=\\\"粗心\\\"...><span class=\\\"tag tag-warn\\\">粗心</span>...`. indexOf(\'粗心\') ≥ 0 definitely...\\n\\nWAIT — maybe the modal that set modalState.html was NOT the wrong modal but something else that happened EARLIER — the detail page test ran BEFORE questions: mastery modal set modalState.html. Then questions mount... click wrong → openWrongModal sets modalState.html again ✓. So html is wrong-modal\'s...\\n\\nHmm hold on, actually — look again: the failure message for 错题原因弹窗缺失 includes `html=<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` — that IS the wrong modal (it uses st-mastery-opt). So modalState.html = wrong modal html. But \'粗心\' indexOf < 0?! \\n\\nOH WAIT. I see it!!! `REASON_TAG_CLASS` — in openWrongModal: `<span class=\\\"tag ${REASON_TAG_CLASS[r]}\\\">${r}</span>` — template literal ✓ contains 粗心. Hmm.\\n\\nLet me look at the actual openWrongModal code I wrote:\\n\\n```js\\nvar opts = REASON_TAGS.map(function (r, i) {\\n  return `<label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt${i === 0 ? \' sel\' : \'\'}\\\">\\n    <input type=\\\"radio\\\" name=\\\"wrong-reason\\\" value=\\\"${r}\\\"${i === 0 ? \' checked\' : \'\'}>\\n    <span class=\\\"tag ${REASON_TAG_CLASS[r]}\\\">${r}</span>\\n    <span class=\\\"ds\\\" style=\\\"margin-left:auto\\\"></span>\\n  </label>`;\\n}).join(\'\');\\n```\\n\\nContains 粗心 multiple times. indexOf(\'粗心\') >= 0. So the check should PASS...\\n\\nUNLESS the html in modalState is NOT from openWrongModal but from a DIFFERENT modal — and the snippet `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` coincidentally matches... What other modal uses st-mastery-opt? The MASTERY modal in detail page: `<label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt...\\\">` with `<input type=\\\"radio\\\" name=\\\"mastery\\\" value=\\\"1\\\">` and `<span class=\\\"nm\\\">未学</span>`. The snippet `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">` + `<input typ...` — truncated. If modalState.html is the MASTERY modal (from the detail test), then \'粗心\' is absent → failure. So the wrong-click did NOT open the wrong modal, and modalState.html still holds the mastery modal from the detail test!\\n\\nSo `click(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q2\\\"] [data-action=\\\"wrong\\\"]\')` did NOT trigger openWrongModal. And q1 toggle expand ALSO didn\'t work. So **questions page click handlers are NOT firing** — confirmed now. Both q1 toggle and wrong action fail; but the \\\"answer\\\" check passed trivially (mask still present → \'答案遮罩未移除\' NOT pushed... wait, if handler didn\'t fire, mask remains → check `if (card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\'))` → true → should push \'答案遮罩未移除\'! It\'s NOT in failures! Hmm!!! \\n\\nSo the ANSWER handler DID fire (mask removed), but TOGGLE and WRONG didn\'t?? Let me recheck... \\n\\nOH WAIT!!! I think I finally see it. The toggle click: `click(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\')` — the toggle button is inside `.st-q-extra` which has `hidden` attribute! **In jsdom, `hidden` elements... `querySelector` still finds them. But `node.click()`** — jsdom click works on hidden elements.\\n\\nHmm, but the answer button is ALSO inside the hidden .st-q-extra! And the answer handler FIRED (mask removed). So clicks inside hidden elements DO work.\\n\\nSo: toggle click → handler → `[data-action=\\\"toggle\\\"]` → `toggleCard(card)` → should add \'expanded\'... but card1 doesn\'t have it. AND the wrong click → openWrongModal should set modalState — didn\'t.\\n\\nWhat if `e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')` returns the WRONG thing... or what if the click on the toggle button... hmm.\\n\\nWAIT A SECOND. Let me look at the toggle button HTML:\\n\\n```html\\n<button class=\\\"st-q-toggle\\\" data-action=\\\"toggle\\\" data-id=\\\"...\\\">展开 ${icon(\'chevron\', 14)}</button>\\n```\\n\\nIn jsdom, `.click()` on button → click event → bubbles to listBox → handler. `btn = e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')` → the button ✓. action=\'toggle\' → `var c = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\'); if (c) toggleCard(c);` → toggleCard adds \'expanded\' to c — c IS card1...\\n\\nHmm — could `card1` in the test be a DIFFERENT element than `c`? No — single q1 card.\\n\\nHmm hmm. What about... the `data-action=\\\"answer\\\"` handler — it worked (mask removed). That\'s INSIDE the same handler function! So the handler fires for answer but not for toggle?! The difference: the toggle button ALSO matches `[data-action]`... \\n\\nOH MY GOD. I see it now!!! `e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')` — the toggle button has data-action=\\\"toggle\\\". But ALSO — WAIT. Let me check `closest` in jsdom — Element.prototype.closest — fine.\\n\\nHmm, what else... Let me look at MY TEST again:\\n\\n```js\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');\\nvar card1 = el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\');\\nif (!card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')) failures.push(\'questions: 卡片展开失败\');\\n```\\n\\n`click(el, sel)` — `el.querySelector(sel)` — jsdom querySelector with `[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]` — fine, returns toggle button.\\n\\n`node.click()` — jsdom\'s HTMLElement.click() — hmm, does jsdom implement click()? YES (it dispatches a click MouseEvent). But — for BUTTON elements inside forms... no form here.\\n\\nHmm, hold on — actually, let me reconsider: does jsdom\'s click() dispatch an event that `e.target` = the button? Yes.\\n\\nOK — empirically debug. But actually — wait. Let me re-read the STEPS log:\\n\\n```\\ntree mounted, cards=2\\nquestions mounted, cards=2\\nwrong mounted, items=3\\nreview1 hidden=false, options=4\\n```\\n\\nReview works! wrong page click handlers FIRE (enterReview worked, options=4). So delegation works in general. The questions page handlers: toggle failed, wrong failed, answer SUCCEEDED. \\n\\nHmm... unless the ANSWER check passed for the wrong reason! `if (card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\'))` — the answer area: `<span class=\\\"st-answer-mask\\\">answer</span><button data-action=\\\"answer\\\">查看答案</button>`. The mask span has class st-answer-mask. If the handler didn\'t fire, mask present → push failure. NOT pushed → handler fired → mask removed. So answer worked!\\n\\nSo in questions, answer works, toggle & wrong don\'t. What distinguishes them? The ANSWER button and the toggle button are BOTH inside `.st-q-extra[hidden]`. The wrong button too. \\n\\nWAIT — the toggle button: `data-action=\\\"toggle\\\"`. The answer button: `data-action=\\\"answer\\\"`. The wrong button: `data-action=\\\"wrong\\\"`. In the handler:\\n\\n```js\\nvar btn = e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\');\\nif (btn) {\\n  var id = btn.dataset.id;\\n  var action = btn.dataset.action;\\n  if (action === \'toggle\') {...}\\n  else if (action === \'answer\') {...}\\n  else if (action === \'wrong\') { openWrongModal(id); }\\n  ...\\n```\\n\\nEverything\'s the same path. UNLESS — `btn.dataset.id` — the toggle button has data-id ✓...\\n\\nHmm, hold on — is it possible that the q1 toggle click threw an exception INSIDE the handler, which jsdom swallows?? No — jsdom propagates listener errors? Actually, listener exceptions in jsdom DO propagate to window error... via dispatchEvent they get caught? When you call element.click(), jsdom dispatches the event SYNCHRONOUSLY; listener exceptions propagate up to the click() caller (they\'re not swallowed). If toggleCard threw, my test\'s try/catch would record \'questions: <msg>\'. Not present.\\n\\nHmm, so toggle handler ran WITHOUT exception but without effect?! toggleCard: `card.classList.toggle(\'expanded\')` — hmm... `var expanded = card.classList.toggle(\'expanded\')` — jsdom classList.toggle(className) — returns true/false and toggles. Then `card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')` — should be true.\\n\\nUNLESS `card` (from `btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')`) is NULL and the `if (c)` guard skipped toggleCard silently! Why would closest fail? The button IS inside .st-q-card... \\n\\nHmm wait — is it?? Let me re-look at cardHTML structure:\\n\\n```html\\n<div class=\\\"glass-card st-q-card\\\" data-qid=\\\"...\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"st-q-stem\\\">...</div>\\n  <div class=\\\"st-q-meta\\\">...</div>\\n  <div class=\\\"st-q-extra\\\" hidden>\\n    <div class=\\\"st-q-options\\\">...</div>\\n    <div class=\\\"st-q-answer\\\">...</div>\\n    <div class=\\\"st-q-analysis\\\" hidden>...</div>\\n    <div class=\\\"st-q-foot\\\">\\n      <button ... data-action=\\\"wrong\\\">...</button>\\n      <button ... data-action=\\\"del\\\">...</button>\\n      <button class=\\\"st-q-toggle\\\" data-action=\\\"toggle\\\">展开 <svg></svg></button>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</div>\\n```\\n\\n`btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')` — should find the div. \\n\\nOK you know what — I wonder if the issue is my click() helper: `el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\')`. In jsdom, `.st-q-toggle` — fine...\\n\\nHmm, actually — WAIT. Let me look at the WRONG-test click: `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — WORKED (review1 options=4). And in questions: `click(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\')` — FAILED. Difference: the questions card clicks happen on elements inside `[hidden]`... but the answer button also inside hidden and it worked.\\n\\nAAAARGH. Let me stop and think about the ANSWER result differently: maybe the answer check passed because `card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\')` returned null for a DIFFERENT reason — because the mask element\'s class was removed... OR because the mask span is `display:none`?? No, querySelector ignores CSS visibility.\\n\\nHmm — OR the whole q1 card\'s innerHTML was replaced between? No.\\n\\nWait wait wait. Actually — let me recheck: does `[data-action=\\\"answer\\\"]` handler remove the mask class? `maskEl.classList.remove(\'st-answer-mask\')` — yes. So if that ran, mask gone.\\n\\nOK here\'s another thought — maybe the toggle click DID toggle, but `card1` lookup... `el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\')` — q1 card. `card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')`...\\n\\nYou know what? Let me just add a probe listener to listBox in the test before clicking, logging every click event target & dataset. And also try `toggleCard` via direct card click (not button). Empirical, quick. Modify the questions test section:\\n\\n```js\\nvar probe = el.querySelector(\'#st-q-list\');\\nvar logClicks = function (e) { log(\'CLICK target=\' + (e.target.className || e.target.tagName) + \' action=\' + (e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\') ? e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\').dataset.action : \'none\')); };\\nprobe.addEventListener(\'click\', logClicks);\\n```\\nThis capture-phase? Listener order: my page handler was added first; probe added second — both fire (bubble phase, same target). Add probe BEFORE clicking.\\n\\nAlso — hmm, actually, hold on. Let me reconsider ONE more time. In the harness, `window.App.icon = function () { return \'<svg></svg>\'; }` — inline svg without xmlns in innerHTML... jsdom parses fine.\\n\\nHmm — but WAIT: `.st-q-toggle` contains the SVG. When jsdom parses `<svg>` via innerHTML — it creates an SVG element in the SVG namespace... and `e.target.closest` — SVGElement.closest exists. But e.target for the click would be the BUTTON anyway.\\n\\nOK — one more consideration: maybe my handler\'s `return;` after `toggle` — no.\\n\\nLet me also reconsider the overview failure: `overview: 数字未滚动到目标值, val=2` — my assertion expected \'1\' but real streak=2 (c1 today, c2 yesterday) — harness expectation bug ✓ (fix to \'2\').\\n\\nAnd wrong: `第三轮选项缺失` — after `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` the panel had... STEPS show: `after-next options=0, exitBtn=true` — after the FIRST next click (from w1 result), options=0 and exitBtn=true → the DONE panel appeared immediately?! That means after answering w1 correctly, clicking next → reviewIdx 1 → w2 should render with options... but options=0 + exitBtn → done panel → reviewIdx was 2 already??\\n\\nLet me trace: queue = [w1, w2] (both non-archived), reviewIdx=0 (w1). Answer A → result. Click next → reviewIdx=1 → renderReview → w2 → options should be 2 (A,B)... but options=0!\\n\\nHmm — unless queue only had [w1]! enterReview: `var all = App.store.wrongQuestions.list().filter(function (w) { return w.status !== \'archived\'; })` — w1 pending ✓, w2 learning ✓ → both. Sorted by nextReview: w1 (today) then w2 (today+2) → [w1, w2]. reviewIdx=0.\\n\\nWait — but the FIRST click was `[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]`... hold on, maybe `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — `el.querySelector(\'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — the FIRST match in DOM order — items rendered: w1, w2, w3 (list order = store order) ✓ w1.\\n\\nHmm, then why options=0 after next?...\\n\\nOH WAIT!!! I see it!!! `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — `review` is the reviewBox element — the button is INSIDE reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\') → `#st-review-next` — `review.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\')` — find the button ✓ click ✓ → `reviewIdx++; renderReview();` → renders w2... \\n\\nUNLESS the click handler for next wasn\'t bound! In submitReview: `var next = box.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\'); if (next) { next.addEventListener(\'click\', function () { reviewIdx++; reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'; renderReview(); }); }` — box = reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\') — the result panel. The button is inside → bound ✓.\\n\\nHmm — but wait, the ORDER: `reviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'[data-review-exit]\').forEach(...)` then next binding — both in the resultHtml block ✓.\\n\\nOK — so why did next → done panel? reviewIdx went from 0 to 1, renderReview: w = reviewQueue[1]... \\n\\n**OH NO. I SEE IT NOW!!!** Look at `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — the click helper:\\n```js\\nfunction click(el, sel) {\\n  var node = el.querySelector(sel);\\n  if (!node) { failures.push(\'找不到元素: \' + sel); return null; }\\n  node.click();\\n  return node;\\n}\\n```\\n`el` = review (reviewBox). The button #st-review-next — BUT the reviewBox ALSO contains, from the FIRST render, `[data-review-exit]` buttons... no conflict with #st-review-next.\\n\\nHmm — but WAIT: does the result panel get REPLACED? After w1 answer, `box.innerHTML = resultHtml` — the OLD options panel (from renderReview) still exists in reviewBox (result panel was appended INTO the options panel\'s sibling #st-review-result div). The old options buttons remain (not removed). So `review.querySelector(\'[data-opt]\')` would still find OLD buttons... but log says after-next options=0!! So the reviewBox content was FULLY replaced → renderReview ran for the DONE case (queue exhausted) → reviewIdx must be ≥ 2.\\n\\nHow? `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` fired ONCE → reviewIdx 0→1 → renderReview(w2)... but log shows options=0 and exitBtn=true → that\'s the DONE panel (has exitBtn; options none). Done panel renders when `!w` i.e. reviewIdx >= queue.length=2. So reviewIdx went 0→2 in one click?? OR the click fired TWICE? `node.click()` once...\\n\\nOR — the done panel is what rendered and the log line `after-next options=0, exitBtn=true` is the DONE panel. So reviewIdx=2 after one next click. That means before the next-click, reviewIdx was 1?? Then the w1 answer didn\'t happen at reviewIdx 0... \\n\\nHmm — OR: `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — enterReview(w1.id). But before that, in the test: `click(el, \'[data-tab=\\\"待复习\\\"]\')` then `click(el, \'[data-tab=\\\"全部\\\"]\')` — tab handlers re-render list ✓ no effect on review.\\n\\nHmm hold on — actually — maybe `enterReview` was called with w1 but... queue = [w1, w2], reviewIdx=0 ✓. renderReview → w1 panel with 4 options (log: options=4 ✓). Answer A → submitReview(w1.id, \'A\', btn) → applyReviewResult → update → archived? consecutive 0→1, status learning ✓ (assertions passed: status learning, consecutive 1, nextReview +2 ✓✓✓ — these PASSED, no failures for them!). Then click next → reviewIdx 1 → renderReview(w2)... \\n\\nHmm wait — the assertions after answering:\\n```\\nif (w1.status !== \'learning\' || ...) — PASSED\\nif (w1.nextReview !== daysFromNow(2)) — PASSED\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');   ← log \'after-next options=0, exitBtn=true\'\\nvar w2opt = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"B\\\"]\');\\n```\\nIf renderReview(w2) ran, options would be 2 (A,B) — log says 0. So renderReview rendered the DONE panel. reviewIdx must be 2 at that point...\\n\\nWAIT — maybe queue = [w1] ONLY! Why? `reviewQueue = all;` — `all = list.filter(w => w.status !== \'archived\')` — w2 is \'learning\' ✓ included. Sort: `(a.nextReview||\'\').localeCompare(b.nextReview||\'\')` — w1 nextReview = today, w2 = today+2 → [w1, w2]. Hmm.\\n\\nHold on — actually, WAIT. What if the SECOND click (`click(review, \'#st-review-next\')`) — the FIRST next click was already done?? No...\\n\\nLet me look at the test flow ONE more time:\\n\\n```js\\nclick(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\');          // enter review w1\\nvar review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\');\\nlog(\'review1 hidden=\' + review.hidden + \', options=\' + review.querySelectorAll(\'[data-opt]\').length);   // options=4 ✓\\nif (review.hidden) ...\\nvar optA = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\');\\nif (!optA) ... else optA.click();          // answer A\\nvar result = review.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\');\\nif (result.textContent.indexOf(\'答对了\') < 0) ...   // PASSED\\nvar w1 = ...; assertions PASSED\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');          // next → should show w2\\nvar w2opt = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"B\\\"]\');\\nif (!w2opt) failures.push(\'wrong: 第二题选项缺失\'); else w2opt.click();\\n```\\n\\nlog: `after-next options=0, exitBtn=true` — WAIT, the log line I added is INSIDE the click(review, \'[data-review-exit]\') section:\\n```js\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');\\nlog(\'after-next options=\' + review.querySelectorAll(\'[data-opt]\').length + \', exitBtn=\' + !!review.querySelector(\'[data-review-exit]\'));\\n```\\nYes — after-next: options=0, exitBtn=true → DONE panel shown → reviewIdx=2.\\n\\nSo after clicking next ONCE from w1 result, reviewIdx became 2. reviewIdx++ → 1 → renderReview → w=reviewQueue[1]... \\n\\nUNLESS reviewQueue was REBUILT between! `enterReview` sets reviewQueue = all. But — the next-click handler: `reviewIdx++; reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'; renderReview();` — doesn\'t rebuild queue.\\n\\nOR — `reviewIdx` was ALREADY 1 when we answered?? No — options=4 was w1\'s question... wait, w1\'s question (q1) has 4 options ✓.\\n\\nHmm — what if the ANSWER click triggered BOTH submitReview AND ... no.\\n\\nWAIT A MINUTE. What if `optA.click()` — the click on `.st-option-btn` — bubbles up to... the options buttons are inside #st-review-options inside reviewBox — no parent handlers except listBox (not ancestor). OK.\\n\\nHmm — what if the next button click ALSO triggered something else... The next button `#st-review-next` is INSIDE #st-review-result — inside reviewBox. reviewBox has no click handler. OK.\\n\\nSo how did reviewIdx jump to 2? ... OR did renderReview get called with w2 but w2 was REMOVED from queue? `renderReview` has the missing-question branch: `var q = linked(w); if (!q) { remove; reviewIdx++; renderReview(); }` — w2 → linked q2 exists ✓.\\n\\nOR — w2 was removed from store?? In the w1 answer, applyReviewResult(w1...) — only w1. Hmm.\\n\\nOR — `reviewQueue[1]` is UNDEFINED because reviewQueue = [w1] only! Then done panel. Why would w2 be excluded? `filter(w => w.status !== \'archived\')` — w2.status = \'learning\'...\\n\\nHmm hold on — wait. Let me check the tab clicks BEFORE: `click(el, \'[data-tab=\\\"待复习\\\"]\')` → tab=\'待复习\' → renderList. `click(el, \'[data-tab=\\\"全部\\\"]\')` → tab=\'全部\'. These don\'t touch wrongQuestions.\\n\\nOK — could `enterReview` have been called TWICE — once for w1 via the item click, and the item click ALSO... no.\\n\\nHmm hmm. Actually — WAIT. Let me reconsider: is it possible the \'答对了\' check passed but the ANSWER was never submitted — i.e., `optA.click()` did nothing, and `#st-review-result` was EMPTY → `result.textContent.indexOf(\'答对了\')` — empty string indexOf → -1 → failure \'wrong: 答对结果未显示\' — NOT in failures... so answer WAS submitted ✓.\\n\\nThen w1 assertions passed ✓. Then next → done panel.\\n\\nSo queue[1] must be undefined... OR reviewIdx was 1 and... renderReview: `var w = reviewQueue[reviewIdx]; if (!w) { done }` — if reviewIdx=1 and queue=[w1] → done ✓. So queue=[w1]. WHY?\\n\\n`enterReview`:\\n```js\\nvar all = App.store.wrongQuestions.list().filter(function (w) { return w.status !== \'archived\'; })\\n  .sort(...);\\nreviewQueue = all;\\nreviewIdx = all.findIndex(w => w.id === id);\\n```\\nw1 pending ✓, w2 learning ✓ — both in `all`...\\n\\nUNLESS — the test\'s earlier actions MODIFIED w2\'s status!! The `questions` test ran BEFORE wrong — it added a wrong record for q2: `store.wrongQuestions.add({questionId:\'q2\', ...})` → new record id \'n-0\' — that\'s a NEW record, w2 unchanged. Hmm — also the questions test DELETED nothing. Wait — the questions test clicked `[data-action=\\\"wrong\\\"]` on q2 → openWrongModal → confirmed → added wrongQuestions record {questionId: \'q2\', status:\'pending\', ...}. So now there are 4 wrong records: w1, w2, w3, n-0(pending). The wrong page test: items = 3 (list shows all 4?? — `el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-wrong-item\').length !== 3` — it PASSED (no failure), so items were 3?? With 4 records, filtered() for \'全部\' returns 4 → items.length 4 ≠ 3 → failure expected! NOT in failures!\\n\\nHmm!! So the questions wrong-click did NOT add the record (consistent with the handler not firing for wrong action!). And \'未生成错题记录\' check: `store.wrongQuestions.list().some(w => w.questionId===\'q2\')` — w2 IS questionId q2!! So that check passes trivially because w2 exists! Bad test assertion (should check a NEW record with status pending & reviewCount 0). OK.\\n\\nSo wrong page has 3 items ✓ (w1,w2,w3 — no new record since questions wrong-click handler didn\'t fire).\\n\\nBack to the mystery: next → done panel. Let me now suspect **the `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` helper clicked a STALE button** — after answering, the result panel has #st-review-next. review = reviewBox (stable). querySelector finds the current one ✓.\\n\\nHmm, hold on — actually — what if `renderReview` was invoked by something ELSE between? The `reviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'[data-review-exit]\')` binding in submitReview — binds exit buttons → exitReview... not called.\\n\\nOK — what about `reviewIdx` being incremented TWICE: the next button handler: `reviewIdx++; reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'; renderReview();`. If the next button were clicked TWICE... `node.click()` fires once.\\n\\nHmm — OR the w1 answer submission happened at reviewIdx=1!! What if `enterReview` set reviewIdx=1?? `all.findIndex(w => w.id === \'w1\')` — if `all` = [w2, w1] sorted... sort by nextReview: w1 nextReview=today, w2 nextReview=today+2 → localeCompare: \'2026-08-03\' < \'2026-08-05\' → w1 first → idx 0.\\n\\nWAIT — actually — what about `w3`?? w3 status archived → excluded ✓.\\n\\nHmm hmm hmm. What about the \'待复习\' tab click — it calls renderList() — the items get RE-RENDERED. Then \'全部\' → renderList again. The [data-review=\\\"w1\\\"] element is fresh ✓. click → enterReview... \\n\\nWAIT!!! I just realized — the tab click handler:\\n```js\\ntabsBox.addEventListener(\'click\', function (e) {\\n  var btn = e.target.closest(\'[data-tab]\');\\n  ...\\n});\\n```\\nAnd listBox click handler separately. `click(el, \'[data-tab=\\\"待复习\\\"]\')` — el=content; button inside tabsBox ✓ → tab=\'待复习\' → renderList → items=1 (w1 pending) ✓ passed. Then \'全部\' → 3 items ✓.\\n\\nThen `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — but wait, there are now potentially MULTIPLE elements matching [data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]? No, one per item.\\n\\nOK I give up guessing; the empirical probe approach is necessary. Let me add probes to the wrong section:\\n- log reviewQueue contents: can\'t access closure... but I CAN log via the DOM: after next, log reviewBox.innerHTML.slice(0,200).\\n- Log reviewIdx via... not accessible.\\n\\nLet me add to the test after clicking next:\\n```js\\nlog(\'after-next html: \' + review.innerHTML.slice(0, 150).replace(/\\\\n/g, \' \'));\\n```\\n\\nAlso for questions: add probe click logger.\\n\\nAND one more hypothesis for the wrong mystery — **`reviewBox.dataset.locked`**: after w1 answer, `reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'1\'` was set in the OPTION click handler... then next handler sets `reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'` ✓.\\n\\nHmm — OH WAIT!!! I think I FINALLY got it!!! Look at the next-click handler binding:\\n\\n```js\\nvar next = box.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\');\\nif (next) {\\n  next.addEventListener(\'click\', function () {\\n    reviewIdx++;\\n    ...\\n  });\\n}\\n```\\n\\nAnd **`box` = `reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\')`** — but WAIT, `reviewBox` is a module-closure variable of the WRONG_DEF.mount — which is stable ✓. `box` = the result div ✓.\\n\\nHmm, that\'s fine. And `#st-review-next` — hmm, but there\'s a subtle issue: **the click on `#st-review-next` BUBBLES UP through reviewBox** — reviewBox has no click listener ✓.\\n\\nOK — what about **`submitReview` being called twice** — the option click handler: `if (reviewBox.dataset.locked === \'1\') return; reviewBox.dataset.locked = \'1\'; ... submitReview(...)`. Once. ✓.\\n\\nAlright — actually, let me look at the \'第三轮选项缺失\' failure + \'连续答对 3 次未归档\' + \'Cannot read properties of null (reading textContent)\':\\n\\n```js\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');      // after w2 answered wrong — next → reviewIdx 2 → done panel\\nlog(...)                               // done panel confirmed: options=0, exitBtn=true\\nclick(review, \'[data-review-exit]\');   // exit → renderList\\nclick(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\');       // re-enter w1\\nreview = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\');\\nvar a1 = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\');\\nif (!a1) failures.push(\'wrong: 重进后选项缺失\'); else a1.click();\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');      // ← hmm, but this line — after answering a1, click next?? \\n```\\n\\nWAIT — look at MY test code in the v2 harness:\\n\\n```js\\nclick(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\');\\nreview = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\');\\nvar a1 = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\');\\nif (!a1) failures.push(\'wrong: 重进后选项缺失\'); else a1.click();\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');\\nvar a2 = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\');\\nif (!a2) failures.push(\'wrong: 第三轮选项缺失\'); else a2.click();\\n```\\n\\nAfter a1.click() (w1 answer → consecutive 2), click next → reviewIdx 1 → w2 rendered... then a2 = w2\'s option A → click → w2 consecutive 2 (learning)... then check w1b.status — w1 consecutive 2 → \'learning\' → \'连续答对 3 次未归档\' FAILURE ✓ (that\'s what we see!). And \'第三轮选项缺失\' — a2 was null → w2 panel didn\'t render → DONE panel again!!! So after re-entering w1 and answering A, clicking next → DONE panel (options=0). So the re-entered queue was [w1] again???\\n\\n**CONSISTENT PATTERN: the queue after answering w1 is always [w1] — w2 never in queue!**\\n\\nWhy would w2 not be in the queue... `filter(w => w.status !== \'archived\')`... w2 status \'learning\'... \\n\\nOH!!!! WAIT!!! I GOT IT!!! `reviewQueue` is a CLOSURE variable in WRONG_DEF.mount — but `enterReview` reads `App.store.wrongQuestions.list()`... **the questions test ran BEFORE wrong test and called `store.wrongQuestions.add({questionId:\'q2\',...})` — NO WAIT, that didn\'t fire (handler issue).\\n\\nHmm — but hold on: the wrong page list showed **3 items** and \'待复习\' filter showed 1 (w1) ✓ — so store has exactly w1,w2,w3 at wrong-test time.\\n\\nSo `all` = [w1, w2]. UNLESS `.filter(function (w) { return w.status !== \'archived\'; })` — hmm... \\n\\n**OHHHH WAIT.** I think I\'ve got it — `App.store.wrongQuestions` in `enterReview` — but what about **`w2.nextReview`** — w2.nextReview = daysFromNow(2) = \'2026-08-05\'. sort by localeCompare — fine.\\n\\nHmm, let me try yet another angle: maybe `enterReview` wasn\'t called at all in the second round! The click on `[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]`... After exitReview, `renderList()` re-rendered items — item w1 exists (status learning now) ✓. click → enterReview(w1.id) — the ITEM CLICK handler:\\n\\n```js\\nlistBox.addEventListener(\'click\', function (e) {\\n  var item = e.target.closest(\'[data-review]\');\\n  if (!item) return;\\n  var w = App.store.wrongQuestions.get(item.dataset.review);\\n  if (!w) return;\\n  if (w.status === \'archived\') { toast; return; }\\n  enterReview(w.id);\\n});\\n```\\nw1 status \'learning\' ✓ → enterReview ✓. Queue = [w1, w2]...\\n\\nHmm, unless — **`w2` was somehow archived** by the wrong-answer in round 1? Round 1: w2 answered B (wrong) → status \'pending\' ✓ (assertion passed: status pending, consecutive 0, nextReview +1 ✓ — no failure for these).\\n\\nSo round 2 queue = [w1(learning), w2(pending)]... \\n\\nYou know what — maybe the issue is with **`review` variable pointing at a STALE reviewBox**! `review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\')` — after exitReview, reviewBox.innerHTML=\'\' and hidden=true. Then re-enter → renderReview sets innerHTML — SAME element (stable). `review` re-queried ✓ same element.\\n\\n`a1 = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\')` — w1 panel → 4 options ✓ (log didn\'t show \'重进后选项缺失\' — so a1 found & clicked). THEN `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — helper finds #st-review-next in the RESULT panel (after answering) → click → reviewIdx++ → renderReview...\\n\\n**WAIT!!! THE ANSWER CLICK — `a1.click()` — the option button ALSO has... hmm, does the OPTION button or the RESULT flow call `reviewIdx++` anywhere?** submitReview → no. OK.\\n\\nAlright — the pattern \\\"next always → done panel\\\" combined with \\\"queue would be [w1,w2]\\\" means `renderReview` sees `reviewQueue[1]` undefined → reviewQueue.length === 1 → `all` had ONE element → w2 was EXCLUDED at enterReview time. When? Round 1 enterReview: w1 pending, w2 learning — both non-archived... \\n\\nUNLESS — **`App.store.wrongQuestions.list()` returns w2 with status \'archived\'**?! Where could w2 be archived... the questions test — didn\'t fire. Hmm — OR the `w3` seed — irrelevant.\\n\\nHmm, actually — hold on. What about `daysFromNow` in the HARNESS being used at wrong-test time — w2.nextReview computed at stub creation ✓.\\n\\nOK — empirical. Add probes:\\n1. In wrong test, before entering review, log store state: `log(\'wrong store: \' + JSON.stringify(store.wrongQuestions.list().map(w=>w.id+\':\'+w.status)))`.\\n2. After clicking next, log `review.innerHTML.slice(0,120)`.\\n\\nLet me also add the questions probe (click logger). Update harness3 and rerun. The install is cached so it\'s quick.\",\"content\":\"剩余失败已收敛。两个疑点需要实证定位：错题复习队列中 w2 未出现（next 直接跳到完成面板）、题库 toggle/wrong 按钮事件未触发（answer 却正常）。在测试中加入探针日志。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"剩余失败已收敛。两个疑点需要实证定位：错题复习队列中 w2 未出现（next 直接跳到完成面板）、题库 toggle/wrong 按钮事件未触发（answer 却正常）。在测试中加入探针日志。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":59,\"round\":59,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":59,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 14:45:31'),
(1472, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 199909, 'tool.started', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', 'call_00_c6hV2rbBmyIWqBbTB9Nk2365', '{\"tool_key\":\"edit_file\",\"display_name\":\"Edit File\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"str_replace\",\"new_str\":\"  /* ---- 4. 题库 ---- */\\n  try {\\n    var el = mountPage(\'/study/questions\');\\n    log(\'questions mounted, cards=\' + el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-q-card\').length);\\n    // 探针：记录 listBox 上的所有点击\\n    el.querySelector(\'#st-q-list\').addEventListener(\'click\', function (e) {\\n      var act = e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\');\\n      log(\'Q-CLICK target=\' + (e.target.tagName || \'\') + \' action=\' + (act ? act.dataset.action : \'none\'));\\n    });\\n    var qcards = el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-q-card\');\\n    if (qcards.length !== 2) failures.push(\'questions: 列表渲染数量错误: \' + qcards.length);\\n    click(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');\\n    var card1 = el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\');\\n    log(\'after toggle expanded=\' + card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\'));\\n    if (!card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')) failures.push(\'questions: 卡片展开失败\');\",\"old_str\":\"  /* ---- 4. 题库 ---- */\\n  try {\\n    var el = mountPage(\'/study/questions\');\\n    log(\'questions mounted, cards=\' + el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-q-card\').length);\\n    var qcards = el.querySelectorAll(\'.st-q-card\');\\n    if (qcards.length !== 2) failures.push(\'questions: 列表渲染数量错误: \' + qcards.length);\\n    click(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');\\n    var card1 = el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\');\\n    if (!card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')) failures.push(\'questions: 卡片展开失败\');\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\study-harness3.js\"},\"effect\":\"write\",\"risk_level\":\"medium\",\"phase\":null,\"operation_id\":null,\"intent\":null,\"shell\":null,\"command_fingerprint\":null}', '2026-08-03 14:45:31'),
