(1496, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 210716, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-63\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Now I have the probe data:\\n\\n**Questions**: `Q-CLICK target=BUTTON action=toggle` fired — the handler received the click with action=toggle. Then `after toggle expanded=false` — the toggle handler ran but the card did NOT get \'expanded\'. The handler code:\\n```js\\nif (action === \'toggle\') {\\n  var c = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\');\\n  if (c) toggleCard(c);\\n}\\n```\\nSo either `btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')` returned null (silently skipped!) or toggleCard didn\'t toggle. toggleCard: `var expanded = card.classList.toggle(\'expanded\');` — should add.\\n\\n**WAIT — I SEE IT NOW!!!** `toggleCard(card)`:\\n```js\\nfunction toggleCard(card) {\\n  var expanded = card.classList.toggle(\'expanded\');\\n  var ex = card.querySelector(\'.st-q-extra\');\\n  if (ex) ex.hidden = !expanded;\\n}\\n```\\nFine... but the click handler for toggle — hmm wait, `action === \'toggle\'` — but look at the probe: `action=toggle` reached the probe (which is a SEPARATE listener on the same element). The probe logs the click happened with action=toggle. But the page handler — was IT also invoked? Both listeners are on listBox. Yes, both run.\\n\\nSo in the page handler: `var btn = e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')` → toggle button; `var action = btn.dataset.action` → \'toggle\'; `var id = btn.dataset.id` → q1; then `if (action === \'toggle\') { var c = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\'); if (c) toggleCard(c); }` → c = the q1 card → toggleCard...\\n\\nThen `card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')` — false!?\\n\\nHmm — jsdom `classList.toggle(\'expanded\')` — returns... **jsdom\'s classList.toggle(className, force) — if force is undefined, toggles and returns true/false** ✓.\\n\\nHmm — could `btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')` return NULL in jsdom because the button is inside... the button IS `.st-q-toggle` inside `.st-q-foot` inside `.st-q-extra` inside `.st-q-card`. closest walks ancestors ✓.\\n\\nOK so WHY didn\'t the class get added?! Let me think about the ANSWER probe: `Q-CLICK target=BUTTON action=answer` — then the check `card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\')` passed (no failure)... \\n\\nHmm wait — the answer handler:\\n```js\\n} else if (action === \'answer\') {\\n  var card = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\');\\n  var maskEl = card.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\');\\n  var ana = card.querySelector(\'.st-q-analysis\');\\n  if (maskEl) { maskEl.classList.remove(\'st-answer-mask\'); maskEl.textContent = \'\'; }\\n  ...\\n```\\nIf `card` were null here → TypeError → caught → \'questions: <msg>\' failure — NOT present. So card was found in the answer path!\\n\\nSo `btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')` works (answer path) — but toggle path didn\'t add the class?!\\n\\nWAIT A SECOND. Let me look at the toggle path ONE more time:\\n\\n```js\\nif (action === \'toggle\') {\\n  var c = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\');\\n  if (c) toggleCard(c);\\n} else if (action === \'answer\') {\\n```\\n\\nHmm — is it possible the toggle click actually went through the CARD-BODY toggle path instead, and my classList check raced? No...\\n\\nHmm — hold on. Let me look at the probe output ORDER:\\n```\\nQ-CLICK target=BUTTON action=toggle     ← q1 toggle click\\nafter toggle expanded=false\\nQ-CLICK target=BUTTON action=answer     ← answer click\\nQ-CLICK target=BUTTON action=toggle     ← q2 toggle click\\nQ-CLICK target=BUTTON action=wrong      ← wrong click\\n```\\n\\nInteresting — \'Q-CLICK target=BUTTON action=toggle\' appears TWICE (q1 toggle + q2 toggle) ✓, answer once ✓, wrong once ✓. All clicks reached listBox. The page handler must also have run (probe is additional listener, both attached to listBox; order: page handler attached FIRST in mount, probe second — both fire).\\n\\nSo for q1 toggle: page handler ran → toggleCard(card) → card.classList.toggle(\'expanded\')... \\n\\nHmm — 