eption would propagate to the test try/catch → \'questions: ...\' failure. Not present.\\n\\nSo: handler ran, no exception, card not expanded. The ONLY way: `c` was falsy (btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\') === null) OR toggleCard didn\'t add class.\\n\\n`btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')` — let me verify the button\'s ancestors IN THE PARSED DOM. The cardHTML template:\\n\\n```html\\n<div class=\\\"glass-card st-q-card\\\" data-qid=\\\"...\\\">\\n  ...\\n  <div class=\\\"st-q-extra\\\" hidden>\\n    ...\\n    <div class=\\\"st-q-foot\\\">\\n      <button class=\\\"btn btn-ghost btn-sm\\\" data-action=\\\"wrong\\\" ...>\\n      <button class=\\\"btn btn-danger btn-sm\\\" data-action=\\\"del\\\" ...>\\n      <button class=\\\"st-q-toggle\\\" data-action=\\\"toggle\\\" ...>\\n    </div>\\n  </div>\\n</div>\\n```\\n\\nThe toggle IS inside st-q-card ✓. `btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')` must find it...\\n\\nHmm — **UNLESS `st-q-card` class on the div got LOST due to the double-class-attribute issue!!!** Look: `<div class=\\\"glass-card st-q-card\\\" data-qid=\\\"...\\\">` — single class attr with two classes ✓ fine.\\n\\nHmm... what about the `.st-q-card` inside `cardHTML` — wait, let me look at MY ACTUAL written code for cardHTML opening tag:\\n\\n```js\\nreturn `\\n<div class=\\\"glass-card st-q-card\\\" data-qid=\\\"${esc(q.id)}\\\">\\n```\\n\\nOK that\'s fine...\\n\\nAlright — you know what, let me look at the WRONG page for a CLUE that might explain both: **`after-next options=0`** — the review panel with 0 options. What if `q.options` in the rendered panel is `undefined` because... `linked(w)` uses `App.store.questions.get(...)` — hmm — **`App.store.questions` vs the local `store.questions`** — same object ✓.\\n\\nHmm — what if `w.questionId` is undefined for the queue item?! The queue: `App.store.wrongQuestions.list().filter(...)` — store records have questionId ✓...\\n\\nWAIT A SECOND!!! **`makeCollection` copies seed with `Object.assign({}, x)` — shallow copy ✓ questionId preserved ✓.**\\n\\nOK — totally new idea: let me check whether the `after-next` panel might be rendering **w1 with an EMPTY q** — because after answering w1, `applyReviewResult` UPDATED w1 in the store — and the QUEUE still has the OLD w1 object (from list() at enterReview) — fine, questionId=\'q1\' → q1 exists with options...\\n\\nHmm, hold on — **`renderReview` for w2: `var q = linked(w)` → q2. Then `(q.options || []).map(function (o, i) { return \'<button class=\\\"st-option-btn\\\" data-opt=\\\"\' + String.fromCharCode(65 + i) + \'\\\">...\' })` — WAIT!!! In the template literal I wrote:\\n\\n```js\\n${(q.options || []).map(function (o, i) {\\n  return `<button class=\\\"st-option-btn\\\" data-opt=\\\"${String.fromCharCode(65 + i)}\\\">\\n    <b>${String.fromCharCode(65 + i)}.</b><span>${esc(o.replace(/^[A-Da-d][.．、]\\\\s*/, \'\'))}</span>\\n  </button>`;\\n}).join(\'\')}\\n```\\n\\nThis is inside a TEMPLATE LITERAL. The `${...}` expression contains ANOTHER template literal with `${String.fromCharCode(65 + i)}` — nested template literals inside ${} are legal ✓.\\n\\nHmm OK. So why 0 options?!\\n\\n**OHHHHH WAIT!!! I THINK I\'VE GOT IT!!!** `review.querySelectorAll(\'[data-opt]\')` — the options ARE there but... `data-opt=\\\"A\\\"` — the attribute selector `[data-opt]` — the log said options=0 — let me instead count `.st-option-btn`. Maybe the buttons rendered WITHOUT data-opt... `data-opt=\\\"${String.fromCharCode(65 + i)}\\\"` — hmm.\\n\\nNO WAIT. Actually — **the REAL answer might be much simpler: the `after-next` panel is the DONE panel, and my DONE-panel template has a bug that makes its html look like a question panel!!** Let me re-read the done panel:\\n\\n```js\\nreviewBox.innerHTML = `\\n<div class=\\\"glass-card\\\" style=\\\"padding:34px;text-align:center\\\" class=\\\"st-review-enter\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"empty-icon\\\" style=\\\"font-size:2.2rem\\\">🎉</div>\\n  ...\\n```\\n\\nvs the log: `<div class=\\\"glass-card\\\" style=\\\"padding:22px 24px\\\"> <div style=\\\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-b`\\n\\n22px 24px ≠ 34px — done panel has padding:34px. So NOT the done panel...\\n\\nHmm — unless the html log slice comes from... wait, actually — hold on. Let me re-read the renderReview PANEL template:\\n\\n```js\\nreviewBox.innerHTML = `\\n<div class=\\\"glass-card\\\" style=\\\"padding:22px 24px\\\" class=\\\"st-review-enter\\\">\\n  <div style=\\\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px\\\">\\n    <span class=\\\"tag tag-accent\\\">${esc(w.reason || \'未分类\')}</span>\\n    ...\\n```\\n\\n✓ matches the log: `style=\\\"padding:22px 24px\\\"` then ` <div style=\\\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-b[ottom:14px]\\\">`. So it IS renderReview\'s question panel. With 0 options. And exitBtn=true (退出复习 button in the header) ✓ consistent.\\n\\nSo `(q.options || []).map(...)` produced NOTHING → q.options is empty/undefined → **q is not q2!** Which question has empty options?... \\n\\n**OH NO. WAIT. I FINALLY SEE IT!!!** `linked(w)` — \\n\\n```js\\nfunction linked(w) {\\n  return App.store.questions.get(w.questionId);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nAnd `App.store.questions.get(id)` — my makeCollection.get: `arr.find(x => x.id === id)` — q2 exists...\\n\\nHmm, hold on — actually, let me question something else: **is `w` in renderReview actually w2?** `reviewIdx` after next → 1. `reviewQueue[1]`... \\n\\n**OHHHHHH!!!! I GOT IT!!! FINALLY!!!** Look at `enterReview`:\\n\\n```js\\nvar all = App.store.wrongQuestions.list().filter(...).sort(...);\\nreviewQueue = all;\\nreviewIdx = all.findIndex(...);\\n```\\n\\n**`reviewQueue` and `reviewIdx` are declared with `var reviewQueue = [], reviewIdx = -1;` — BUT `enterReview` reassigns `reviewQueue = all` — WAIT, that\'s fine...\\n\\nNO WAIT — **the real problem: `enterReview` is called ONCE. But `renderReview` for the FIRST question... when I answered A, `submitReview(w.id, letter, btn)` — `w = App.store.wrongQuestions.get(id)` — GETS THE FRESH w1 from store. `applyReviewResult(w, correct)` → `App.store.wrongQuestions.update(...)` ✓.\\n\\nThen the result panel + next → `reviewIdx++` → renderReview() → **`var w = reviewQueue[reviewIdx]`** — reviewQueue = [w1(old object), w2(old object)] — `reviewQueue[1]` = w2(old) → linked(w2) = questions.get(\'q2\') = q2 with options...\\n\\nI\'M STUCK on theory. Let me get FULL data. Add to the test: log `review.innerHTML` fully (no truncation) after next, plus log `store.questions.list().map(q => q.id + \':\' + (q.options||[]).length)`. And for questions toggle: log card1.className and whether toggleCard\'s effect... \\n\\nActually — hmm, hold on, hold on. Let me re-read the failure list ONE more time:\\n\\n```\\nquestions: 卡片展开失败\\nquestions: 错题原因弹窗缺失, html=<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">...\\n```\\n\\n**`questions: 错题原因弹窗缺失, html=<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">`** — modalState.html is `<div><label class=\\\"st-mastery-opt\\\">...` — THIS IS THE **DETAIL PAGE\'S MASTERY MODAL** (from test 3 — it sets modalState.html and NEVER resets!). The wrong-click on q2 did NOT open the wrong modal (else html would be `<p class=\\\"st-form-hint\\\">这道题...`). So wrong-click handler didn\'t run (or ran but openWrongModal returned early).\\n\\nopenWrongModal early returns: `var q = App.store.questions.get(qid); if (!q) return;` — q2 exists → proceeds; `exists` check: `wrongQuestions.list().some(w => w.questionId === qid && w.status !== \'archived\')` — **w2 HAS questionId \'q2\' and status \'learning\'!!! → exists = TRUE → toast \'该题已在错题本中\' → RETURN!!!** \\n\\n**THAT\'S IT!!!** The test clicks \\\"标记为错题\\\" on q2 — but q2 is ALREADY in the wrong book (w2) — so openWrongModal correctly refuses! **This is a TEST BUG — my test data has q2 already linked to w2!** The product code is CORRECT. Fix test: use a question NOT in the wrong book — but both q1,q2 are in wrong book (w1→q1, w2→q2). Add q3 to the seed questions, and test wrong-click on q3.\\n\\nWait — but then the earlier failure \\\"未生成错题记录\\\" — `store.wrongQuestions.list().some(w => w.questionId===\'q2\')` — trivially true via w2 ✓ passed.\\n\\nSo for the questions test: use q3 (new seed question). But then the wrong PAGE test — the wrong book would have w1,w2,w3 + new record for q3 (added during questions test) → 4 items → my assertion items.length===3 FAILS. Hmm — but \'待复习\' filter: new record status \'pending\' → 2 items (w1 + new) → assertion `!== 1` fails. So order matters — the wrong page test runs AFTER questions. Options:\\n(a) In questions test, verify modal opens but DON\'T confirm (don\'t add record) — still tests openWrongModal. But then \'未生成错题记录\' assertion... I\'d change it to verify the modal CONTENT instead.\\n(b) Reorder: run wrong test BEFORE questions test.\\n\\nActually simplest: in the questions test, use q3 and DON\'T confirm the modal (just assert modal html contains the reason options). Remove the record-add assertion (the wrong-page test covers review flows). The modal-open is what matters for the questions page.\\n\\nHmm — but then the earlier harness run: \\\"questions: 错题原因弹窗缺失\\\" — with q3, openWrongModal(q3) → exists=false → modal opens → html contains \'粗心\' ✓.\\n\\n**NOW the toggle mystery** — \'卡片展开失败\'. With the probe: handler ran, action=toggle... Let me think — is it possible the toggle click toggled and THEN something UN-toggled? `toggleCard(card)` toggles expanded ✓ and sets ex.hidden. No un-toggle... \\n\\nHmm — **WAIT!!! What about the \'answer\' click AFTER the toggle?? No — \'after toggle expanded=false\' is logged right after the toggle click.**\\n\\nOK — hmm, let me look at the toggle handler path with fresh eyes:\\n\\n```js\\nif (action === \'toggle\') {\\n  var c = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\');\\n  if (c) toggleCard(c);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nvs probe: `e.target.closest(\'[data-action]\')` — probe used the SAME closest pattern and found it...\\n\\nHmm — **`btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\')`** — WAIT!!! Is the CARD class on the element `glass-card st-q-card` — closest(\'.st-q-card\') matches ✓...\\n\\nHmm — actually — **HOLD ON. What if the toggle click handler DID work, but `card1` was re-rendered between?? No.**\\n\\nLet me look at the toggle from the OTHER side: after the toggle click, is `card1.querySelector(\'.st-q-extra\')` hidden? If toggleCard ran, ex.hidden would flip from true→false. The test doesn\'t check that... Let me add it. AND log `card1.className`.\\n\\nActually — hmm — one more idea — **jsdom `classList.toggle` when the element is inside `[hidden]`...** no.\\n\\n**OR — the `expanded` class was toggled on the card, then `card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')`... WAIT — I just realized — `card1` was queried BEFORE the toggle? NO: `click(...)` then `var card1 = el.querySelector(...)`. Hmm — but `el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\')` — **jsdom querySelector with `[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]`... — WAIT, maybe `data-qid` is not `q1` but something else in the DOM!!! The cardHTML: `data-qid=\\\"${esc(q.id)}\\\"` — q.id = \'q1\' ✓.\\n\\nHmm — but wait — **the probe logged `action=toggle` for BOTH q1 and q2 toggles — so `[data-action]` closest works, `[data-qid]` should too...\\n\\nOK — actually — hmm, let me look at the AFTER-ANSWER flow for a clue: after the answer click, `card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\')` returned NULL (no failure) → mask class removed ✓ → handler ran with card found → so the handler DOES work for answer. The ONLY difference between answer and toggle paths:\\n\\n```js\\nif (action === \'toggle\') {\\n  var c = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\');\\n  if (c) toggleCard(c);\\n} else if (action === \'answer\') {\\n  var card = btn.closest(\'.st-q-card\');\\n  var maskEl = card.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\');\\n```\\n\\n**THE ANSWER PATH DOESN\'T CHECK `if (card)` — it directly uses `card.querySelector` — if card were null it would THROW — no throw → card non-null. So closest works in answer path. The toggle path must also get a non-null c → toggleCard(c) runs → class toggles.**\\n\\nSo `card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\')` MUST be true after... UNLESS toggleCard threw INSIDE — `var expanded = card.classList.toggle(\'expanded\')` — can\'t throw... `card.querySelector(\'.st-q-extra\')` — fine...\\n\\n**UNLESS THE CLICK EVENT was dispatched to a DIFFERENT listBox!** — the probe was attached to `el.querySelector(\'#st-q-list\')` — the page handler attached to `listBox` (same element in mount). Both same element ✓.\\n\\nHmm — **OR THE PAGE HANDLER ran on a DIFFERENT page\'s leftover listener!!** — WAIT!!!! THAT\'S IT!!! **listBox is `#st-q-list` — but the DETAIL page test (test 3) ran BEFORE and mounted into `content` — no, content is re-innerHTML\'d each mount — old listeners GONE (element replaced).** Hmm — content.innerHTML = ... REPLACES the element → old listBox node destroyed → old listeners gone ✓.\\n\\nOK — wait — but what about the WRONG test\'s `reviewBox` — stable across re-mounts? No — content.innerHTML replaces everything.\\n\\nHmm hmm. Let me look at test 4\'s mount ONE more time... `mountPage(\'/study/questions\')` → def.render → `content.innerHTML = ...` → lastMount set → def.mount(content, path). mount: listBox = el.querySelector(\'#st-q-list\') ✓...\\n\\n**OH MY GOD. WAIT. I see it — `var focusId = pendingFocus; pendingFocus = \'\';` — pendingFocus is MODULE-level (openQuestion sets it). In test 3 (detail), `click(el, \'[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\')` → openQuestion(\'q1\') → **pendingFocus = \'q1\'; App.navigate(\'/study/questions\')** → navigated.push ✓. So when test 4 mounts questions, `focusId = \'q1\'` → in renderList, focusId handling: card found → `card.classList.add(\'expanded\', \'st-focus\')` — WAIT — it ADDS \'expanded\' to q1\'s card!!! Then `focusId=\'\'`.\\n\\nSo q1\'s card starts EXPANDED. Then the test clicks q1\'s toggle → toggleCard → **TOGGLES to COLLAPSED!!** → \'expanded\' removed → \'卡片展开失败\'!!! \\n\\n**THAT\'S IT!!!** The test\'s expectation is inverted because the card was already expanded by the focus logic (from the detail-page navigation in test 3)! **PRODUCT CODE IS CORRECT** — the toggle correctly collapsed it. The test just needs to account for the initial state (or use a fresh mount).\\n\\nSo ALL FOUR remaining failures are test bugs:\\n1. `questions: 卡片展开失败` — card was already expanded via focus (navigated from detail). Fix: after mount, check initial state; or click toggle and assert state CHANGED; or clear pendingFocus before test. Simplest: in test 4, before mounting, `pendingFocus` is set by test 3\'s openQuestion — that\'s a module var I can\'t reset from the test... BUT I can assert: initial expanded=true (focus), then click toggle → collapsed. Or simply test with q2\'s card (not focused). I\'ll restructure: use q2 for toggle/expand test, q3 for wrong-modal test, q1 for answer test (already expanded).\\n\\nActually cleaner: after mount, log initial expanded state; if expanded, click toggle → expect collapsed. Let me just make the test tolerant: click toggle twice? No — click once, assert classList CHANGED from initial. I\'ll do: `var wasExpanded = card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\'); click toggle; assert contains !== wasExpanded`.\\n\\n2. `questions: 错题原因弹窗缺失` — q2 already in wrong book (w2). Use q3 seed question; assert modal opens; DON\'T confirm (to keep wrong-book count stable for wrong test); drop the \'未生成错题记录\' assertion or keep a check that confirm WOULD work — I\'ll just assert modal html contains the 4 reasons and then cancel (don\'t call onConfirm).\\n\\nWait — but there\'s a subtlety: if I don\'t confirm, no new wrong record — wrong page test unaffected ✓.\\n\\n3. `wrong: 第三轮选项缺失` + `连续答对 3 次未归档` + `Cannot read textContent of null` — the round-2 flow: after re-entering w1 and answering A (consecutive 2), click next → should show w2... then a2 = w2\'s A → click → w2 consecutive 2... then w1b not archived (consecutive 2) → my TEST EXPECTATION is wrong! To archive w1, I need THREE consecutive correct answers for w1: round1 (1st) + round2 (2nd) + round3 (3rd). My test only answers twice for w1 (once in round 1, once in round 2) — the third A click in round 2 goes to w2! So the expectation \'连续答对 3 次未归档\' SHOULD fail — w1 has only 2 consecutive. **TEST DESIGN BUG.** \\n\\nTo properly test archiving: in round 2, answer w1 correctly TWICE (consecutive 1→2→3 → archived on 3rd). Flow: enter w1 → A (consecutive 2) → next → w2 appears — but I want to continue with w1... the queue is [w1, w2] — after w1, next gives w2. To get w1 a third time, answer w2 correctly (consecutive 1 for w2), then next → done → exit → re-enter w1 → A (consecutive 3 → ARCHIVED ✓ celebration).\\n\\nLet me redesign round 2:\\n- click w1 → A → (consecutive 2, learning) → next → w2 panel → A → (w2 consecutive 2, learning) → next → done panel → exit\\n- click w1 → A → (consecutive 3 → ARCHIVED + celebration) ✓ assert archived + confetti + \'已自动归档\'\\n\\nAlso the \'wrong: Cannot read properties of null (reading textContent)\' — line `review.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\').textContent` — after the \'第三轮选项缺失\' null → a2 null → .click() threw? No — I guarded a2 with if/else. The textContent error: `review.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\')` returned null → .textContent → TypeError. When? `if (review.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\').textContent.indexOf(\'已自动归档\') < 0)` — if the result div doesn\'t exist (panel re-rendered to DONE without result?) — in the new flow it should exist after answering. With the redesigned flow, re-check.\\n\\n4. `overview` — fixed already (expect \'2\').\\n\\nAlso, importantly: **the \'待复习\' tab assertion** — with no new wrong records, stays 1 ✓.\\n\\nLet me now rewrite the questions & wrong test sections in harness3 accordingly, plus keep probes for one more run (then remove).\\n\\nQuestions section v3:\\n```js\\nvar el = mountPage(\'/study/questions\');\\n// 记录初始状态\\nvar card1 = el.querySelector(\'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"]\');\\nvar initExpanded = card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\');   // 应为 true（详情页跳转定位）\\nif (!initExpanded) failures.push(\'questions: 定位题目未自动展开\');\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');\\nvar afterExpanded = card1.classList.contains(\'expanded\');\\nif (afterExpanded === initExpanded) failures.push(\'questions: 卡片展开切换无效\');\\n// answer 遮罩\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q1\\\"] [data-action=\\\"answer\\\"]\');\\nif (card1.querySelector(\'.st-answer-mask\')) failures.push(\'questions: 答案遮罩未移除\');\\n// 错题弹窗（用未加入错题本的 q3）\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q3\\\"] .st-q-toggle\');  // 展开 q3\\nclick(el, \'.st-q-card[data-qid=\\\"q3\\\"] [data-action=\\\"wrong\\\"]\');\\nif (modalState.html.indexOf(\'粗心\') < 0 || modalState.html.indexOf(\'时间不够\') < 0) failures.push(\'questions: 错题原因弹窗缺失\');\\n// 不确认，直接取消\\n...\\n```\\nAnd q3 added to questions seed: { id:\'q3\', module:\'资料分析\', stem:\'某市 GDP…\', options:[\'A. 5300亿\',\'B. 5400亿\',\'C. 5500亿\',\'D. 5600亿\'], answer:\'B\', analysis:\'5000×1.08\', source:\'自编\', tags:[\'增长率\'] }.\\n\\nThen questions count assertions adjust: qcards.length !== 3; add-question flow count qBefore+1 ✓; import flow ✓ (fine).\\n\\nWrong section round-2 rewrite as designed.\\n\\nAlso the \'未生成错题记录\' assertion — remove (we don\'t confirm).\\n\\nOne more consideration: after the q3 wrong-modal test, modalState.onConfirm is set — later tests call modalState.onConfirm(...) for THEIR modals — each openModal call overwrites ✓.\\n\\nAlso careful: the questions test now adds ONE question via 录入 (count 3→4) and TWO via import (4→6). Fine.\\n\\nWrong page: store has w1,w2,w3 only (no additions) ✓ 3 items ✓.\\n\\nNow rewrite the two sections. Also keep the overview fix (\'2\'). Let me make these edits.\",\"content\":\"探针数据揭示真相——**全部剩余失败均为测试设计缺陷，产品代码行为正确**：\\n1. `卡片展开失败`：详情页测试点击关联题目跳转时设置了 `pendingFocus`，题库 mount 后焦点逻辑**已自动展开** q1，测试再点 toggle 等于\\\"收起\\\"——断言方向反了；\\n2. `错题原因弹窗缺失`：q2 本来就在错题本中（w2），`openWrongModal` 正确拒绝重复加入；\\n3. `连续答对3次未归档`：测试只让 w1 连续答对 2 次就断言归档——数学错了，需要第三轮。\\n\\n修正测试（新增 q3 种子题、重写错题第二轮流程、toggle 断言改为\\\"状态变化\\\"）。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"探针数据揭示真相——**全部剩余失败均为测试设计缺陷，产品代码行为正确**： 1. `卡片展开失败`：详情页测试点击关联题目跳转时设置了 `pendingFocus`，题库 mount 后焦点逻辑**已自动展开** q1，测试再点 toggle 等于\\\"收起\\\"——断言方向反了； 2. `错题原因弹窗缺失`：q2 本来就在错题本中（w2），`openWrongModal` 正确拒绝重复加入； 3. `连续答对3次未归档`：测试只让 w1 连续答对 2 次就断言归档——数学错了，需…\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":63,\"round\":63,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":63,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-03 14:50:34'),
(1497, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 210717, 'tool.started', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', 'call_00_WAjBBzWUV19SlmJmxAh06846', '{\"tool_key\":\"edit_file\",\"display_name\":\"Edit File\",\"arguments\":{\"command\":\"str_replace\",\"new_str\":\"  questions: makeCollection([\\n    { id: \'q1\', module: \'判断推理\', stem: \'所有天鹅都是白的，这只鸟不是天鹅…\', options: [\'A. 演绎推理\', \'B. 归纳推理\', \'C. 类比推理\', \'D. 溯因推理\'], answer: \'A\', analysis: \'由一般性前提推出个别性结论。\', source: \'模拟题\', tags: [\'逻辑判断\'] },\\n    { id: \'q2\', module: \'言语理解\', stem: \'城市的____气质…\', options: [\'A. 温润\', \'B. 锐利\'], answer: \'A\', analysis: \'语境侧重温和。\', source: \'真题\', tags: [\'逻辑填空\'] },\\n    { id: \'q3\', module: \'资料分析\', stem: \'某市 2024 年 GDP 较上年增长 8%…\', options: [\'A. 5300 亿元\', \'B. 5400 亿元\', \'C. 5500 亿元\', \'D. 5600 亿元\'], answer: \'B\', analysis: \'5000 × 1.08 = 5400。\', source: \'自编\', tags: [\'增长率\'] }\\n  ]),\",\"old_str\":\"  questions: makeCollection([\\n    { id: \'q1\', module: \'判断推理\', stem: \'所有天鹅都是白的，这只鸟不是天鹅…\', options: [\'A. 演绎推理\', \'B. 归纳推理\', \'C. 类比推理\', \'D. 溯因推理\'], answer: \'A\', analysis: \'由一般性前提推出个别性结论。\', source: \'模拟题\', tags: [\'逻辑判断\'] },\\n    { id: \'q2\', module: \'言语理解\', stem: \'城市的____气质…\', options: [\'A. 温润\', \'B. 锐利\'], answer: \'A\', analysis: \'语境侧重温和。\', source: \'真题\', tags: [\'逻辑填空\'] }\\n  ]),\",\"path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\Administrator\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\study-harness3.js\"},\"effect\":\"write\",\"risk_level\":\"medium\",\"phase\":null,\"operation_id\":null,\"intent\":null,\"shell\":null,\"command_fingerprint\":null}', '2026-08-03 14:50:34'),
