(1527, '40122540-fcbb-4890-9b07-1296c60efc8f', 217640, 'agent.turn.completed', 'code', 'moonya', 'pages_study', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"pages_study-turn-68\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"Progress! Questions section all pass now. Wrong section:\\n\\n**`wrong: 第二轮状态错误: {\\\"id\\\":\\\"w1\\\",...,\\\"consecutive\\\":1,...}`** — In round 2, I clicked w1\'s item → answered A → w1.consecutive should be 2 (was 1 from round 1). But it stayed 1!!! \\n\\nWhy? Round 2 flow: `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` → enterReview(w1.id) → queue = [w2(pending, nextReview+1), w1(learning, +2)] sorted → [w2, w1] → reviewIdx = index of w1 = 1 → renderReview → w1 panel → `r2a = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\')` — **WAIT — the panel shows w1\'s question (q1, 4 options A-D)** → r2a click → A → correct → submitReview(\'w1\', \'A\') → applyReviewResult → consecutive 2...\\n\\nBut result shows consecutive stayed 1! So the click didn\'t apply — OR the click hit a DIFFERENT panel. Hmm — actually wait: `review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\')` re-queried ✓. r2a found ✓ clicked ✓. Then w1.consecutive === 1 — not updated!\\n\\nHmm — did submitReview fail? `var w = App.store.wrongQuestions.get(id); var q = linked(w); if (!w || !q) return;` — w1 exists, q1 exists → proceed... `var correct = \'A\' === \'A\'` ✓ → `applyReviewResult(w1, true)` → update → consecutive 2...\\n\\nUNLESS the option click handler didn\'t fire because **`reviewBox.dataset.locked === \'1\'`** — was it left locked from round 1?? In round 1, after the last answer, locked=\'1\' was set (in the option click handler). The next-button handler resets it: `reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'` — round 1\'s next clicked → reset ✓. But wait — round 1\'s LAST answer was w2\'s B (wrong) → locked=\'1\'. Then test clicked `#st-review-next` → handler: reviewIdx++ → **locked=\'\'** ✓ → done panel. Then exit.\\n\\nRound 2: enter w1 → renderReview — **`reviewBox.dataset.locked`** — hmm, renderReview doesn\'t reset locked! It was reset by the next click in round 1 ✓ (\'\' → falsy). So option click → not locked → proceed...\\n\\nHmm wait, actually — look at the round-1 end state: after w2\'s wrong answer → result panel (in #st-review-result) → next clicked → done panel. reviewBox.dataset.locked = \'\' ✓ (set in next handler). Then exitReview → reviewBox.innerHTML=\'\'. Round 2 enter → renderReview → new panel. Option click → locked check: \'\' → proceed ✓.\\n\\nSo why didn\'t consecutive update?!\\n\\n**WAIT — maybe the round-2 click on `[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]` didn\'t enter review at all!** `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — the listBox... after round 1\'s exitReview, renderList re-rendered items — w1 element fresh ✓. Click → enterReview(w1) ✓...\\n\\nHmm — but then `r2a` (found in review panel) — if enterReview DIDN\'T run, reviewBox would be EMPTY (innerHTML=\'\' from exitReview) → r2a null → \'第二轮选项缺失\' failure — NOT present! So enterReview ran, w1 panel rendered, r2a clicked...\\n\\nBut consecutive stayed 1. So submitReview didn\'t update?? OR the update was REVERTED — **`applyReviewResult` — let me re-read it:\\n\\n```js\\nfunction applyReviewResult(w, correct) {\\n  var reviewCount = (Number(w.reviewCount) || 0) + 1;\\n  var consecutive = correct ? (Number(w.consecutive) || 0) + 1 : 0;\\n  ...\\n  return App.store.wrongQuestions.update(w.id, {...});\\n}\\n```\\n\\nw = store.get(\'w1\') at submit time: consecutive 1 → +1 = 2 ✓ update ✓...\\n\\nHmm — **UNLESS the option click handler hit the LOCKED path**: `if (reviewBox.dataset.locked === \'1\') return;` — if locked was still \'1\'... when was it last set? Round 1: option clicks set locked=\'1\' after first click; next handler resets to \'\'. Round 1 sequence: w1 A (locked=\'1\') → next (locked=\'\') → w2 B (locked=\'1\') → next (locked=\'\') → done. So locked=\'\' at round-1 end ✓.\\n\\nRound 2: enter → renderReview → click A → NOT locked → submitReview... \\n\\nHmm hold on — wait. Let me look at the FAILURE LIST once more: **`找不到元素: #st-review-next`** — this came from `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` in round 2 (after r2a). The button not found → meaning the result panel didn\'t render → **submitReview didn\'t run!** So the option click was BLOCKED or the handler didn\'t fire.\\n\\nSo in round 2, the option click didn\'t trigger submitReview. Why? **`reviewBox.dataset.locked`** must be \'1\'!! When? Round 1\'s LAST answer (w2 B wrong) set locked=\'1\'... then `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — **THE NEXT BUTTON — did that click actually fire?** In round 1, after w2\'s wrong answer, the test does `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — button exists in result panel ✓ → handler: `reviewIdx++; reviewBox.dataset.locked=\'\'; renderReview();` — renders DONE panel — the \'已归档筛选错误\' failure at the end suggests... wait let me check the round-1 assertions: \'答错结果未显示\' NOT in failures → w2\'s wrong result panel rendered ✓. Then `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — the button — hmm, was there an issue: the round-2 failure says \'找不到元素: #st-review-next\' — that\'s round 2\'s next click. And \'第二轮状态错误 consecutive 1\' means round-2\'s r2a click DIDN\'T apply.\\n\\nSo in round 2, r2a click was blocked by `locked === \'1\'`. Which means round 1 left locked=\'1\' — the round-1 next click did NOT reset it — **because the round-1 next click DIDN\'T FIRE the handler!** But the DONE panel appeared (round-2\'s review query found... hmm wait, actually in round 2, after exit & re-enter, reviewBox got new innerHTML from renderReview — so we can\'t tell if round-1\'s next worked).\\n\\nHmm — wait, but if round-1\'s next click hadn\'t fired, the panel would still show w2\'s result (not done panel) — then `click(review, \'[data-review-exit]\')` — the result panel HAS [data-review-exit] ✓ (返回错题本 button in result panel!) → exitReview → round 2 enter → w1 panel ✓. So round-1\'s next click MAY have been swallowed!\\n\\nWhy would `#st-review-next` click not fire in round 1? **BECAUSE THE BUTTON IS `disabled`?? No... OR because jsdom click on a button inside... hmm.\\n\\nWAIT — I think I see it now!!! **`click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — `review` = reviewBox — `review.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\')` — in round 1, after w1\'s answer, `box.innerHTML = resultHtml` where `box = reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\')`. The resultHtml contains `#st-review-next`. So review.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\') → found ✓ clicked ✓...\\n\\nHmm — but WAIT — actually let me reconsider: **was the \'答对了\'/\'答错了\' result really rendered in round 1?** \'答对结果未显示\' and \'答错结果未显示\' NOT in failures → yes rendered. So next button existed and was clicked...\\n\\nOK so why is locked still \'1\' in round 2?? Let me re-trace the locked lifecycle VERY carefully:\\n\\nOption click handler:\\n```js\\nreviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'.st-option-btn\').forEach(function (btn) {\\n  btn.addEventListener(\'click\', function () {\\n    if (reviewBox.dataset.locked === \'1\') return;\\n    reviewBox.dataset.locked = \'1\';\\n    reviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'.st-option-btn\').forEach(function (b) { b.classList.remove(\'selected\'); });\\n    btn.classList.add(\'selected\');\\n    var letter = btn.dataset.opt;\\n    submitReview(w.id, letter, btn);\\n  });\\n});\\n```\\n\\nNext handler:\\n```js\\nnext.addEventListener(\'click\', function () {\\n  reviewIdx++;\\n  reviewBox.dataset.locked = \'\';\\n  renderReview();\\n});\\n```\\n\\nRound 1: w1 A → locked \'1\' → submit ✓. next → locked \'\' → done?? NO — reviewIdx 0→1 → w2 panel. Then w2 B → locked \'1\' → submit ✓. next → locked \'\' → reviewIdx 2 → done panel. exit → round 2: enter → renderReview → locked \'\' ✓ → r2a → submit → consecutive 2...\\n\\nHmm — everything checks out IF the clicks fired. But observed: consecutive stayed 1 → r2a\'s submit didn\'t run → locked was \'1\' at that point → so round-1\'s LAST next click didn\'t reset → **round-1\'s second `#st-review-next` click didn\'t fire!**\\n\\nWhy would the second next click fail but the first succeed?? ... \\n\\n**OHHHH WAIT!!!** I think I\'ve got it — **the SECOND next click: `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — BUT at that point, the panel had been REPLACED by renderReview(w2) — the NEXT button from w1\'s result is GONE; the w2 panel has NO #st-review-next until w2 is answered. So the sequence:**\\n\\n1. w1 A → result panel (has #st-review-next) ✓\\n2. `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` → reviewIdx 1 → renderReview(w2) — new panel (options only, NO result yet — no #st-review-next!)\\n3. `w2opt = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"B\\\"]\')` → w2\'s B → click → **locked already \'1\' from step... NO — the next handler reset locked=\'\' in step 2.** Then w2 B click → locked \'1\' → submit ✓ → result panel with #st-review-next.\\n4. `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` (round-1 second next) → reviewIdx 2 → DONE panel. locked=\'\'.\\n\\nThen round 2 works... UNLESS step 4\'s click hit a STALE button?? `review.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\')` — after step 3, the result panel exists with the button → found → click → handler → done ✓.\\n\\nHmm!!! But observed round-2 locked... \\n\\nWAIT — actually — hold on. Let me reconsider step 2: after w1\'s answer, `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — **which button does querySelector find?** After w1\'s answer, reviewBox contains: [panel: options (old), result div with resultHtml]. `#st-review-next` is in resultHtml ✓ unique ✓.\\n\\nHmm OK — so why is consecutive 1 after round 2\'s answer?...\\n\\n**LET ME QUESTION `reviewBox.dataset.locked` IN ROUND 2 ENTER:** `enterReview` — does it reset locked? NO! renderReview doesn\'t either. Round-1 end: after the second next → locked=\'\'. Hmm.\\n\\n**OR — THE REAL CULPRIT: `renderReview`\'s option-click binding happens INSIDE renderReview — but ROUND 2\'s enterReview... wait, r2a click — the binding: `reviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'.st-option-btn\').forEach(bind)` — bound at renderReview time ✓.\\n\\nHmm hmm hmm. Let me look at the OTHER new failure: **\'wrong: 已归档筛选错误\'** — after round 3, `click(el, \'[data-tab=\\\"已归档\\\"]\')` → expected 2 (w3 + w1), but the tab click... el is content — the tabsBox — click [data-tab=\\\"已归档\\\"] → tab=\'已归档\' → renderList → filtered: archived → w3 (archived) + w1 — if w1 NOT archived → 1 item → \'已归档筛选错误\' ✓ consistent with w1 not being archived.\\n\\nAnd \'归档庆祝文案缺失\' + \'庆祝微动效缺失\' — round 3\'s answer didn\'t archive w1 (consecutive stayed 1!!) — wait, round 3 failure message shows w1: consecutive 1, reviewCount 2. So round-2 AND round-3 answers both did NOT apply! Only round-1\'s applied (reviewCount 2 = 1+1 from round 1; consecutive 1).\\n\\nSo after round 1, ALL subsequent option clicks were blocked → **`reviewBox.dataset.locked` stayed \'1\' after round 1!**\\n\\nWhich means round-1\'s flow: w1 A (locked=\'1\') → next (locked=\'\') → w2 B (locked=\'1\') → next → **DID NOT fire** → locked stays \'1\' → done panel NOT shown... but then `click(review, \'[data-review-exit]\')` — w2\'s result panel HAS [data-review-exit] ✓ → exit worked ✓. Round 2 enter → panel → r2a click → locked===\'1\' → BLOCKED ✓✓✓ — **THIS MATCHES!**\\n\\nSo: **round-1\'s SECOND next click did not fire.** Why? Because after w2\'s answer... wait — NO. Let me recheck: round-1 second next — hmm — the test code:\\n\\n```js\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');          // (A) after w1 answer\\nvar w2opt = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"B\\\"]\');\\nif (!w2opt) ... else w2opt.click();        // w2 wrong\\n...assertions...\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');          // (B) after w2 answer — THIS ONE\\n```\\n\\nAt (B): w2\'s result panel has #st-review-next ✓ → click → handler → reviewIdx++ → locked=\'\' → done panel...\\n\\nHmm — but if it fired, locked=\'\'. Observed locked=\'1\' → (B) didn\'t fire its handler OR the handler... \\n\\n**OHHHHH WAIT!!!** I see it — **the (B) click found the button but the button was from the FIRST panel\'s result — NO... hmm.\\n\\nHold on — let me reconsider (A): at (A), reviewIdx 0→1, locked=\'\', renderReview(w2) — the w2 panel. But wait — did (A) actually fire? If (A) fired: w2 panel rendered → w2opt found ✓ (it was found — \'第二题选项缺失\' not in failures) → B clicked → submit ✓ (assertions passed) → result panel. (B) click → fire? If (B) fired → done panel + locked=\'\' → round 2 would work. It didn\'t work → (B) didn\'t fire.\\n\\nWHY would (B) not fire when (A) did?! Both are `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` with a fresh button...\\n\\n**MAYBE BECAUSE THE RESULT PANEL\'S BUTTON IS THE *SAME NODE* AS BEFORE?? NO — innerHTML replaced.**\\n\\nHmm — wait — maybe (B)\'s button click DID fire, but the handler was bound to a STALE closure... The next binding:\\n```js\\nvar next = box.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\');\\nif (next) {\\n  next.addEventListener(\'click\', function () {\\n    reviewIdx++;\\n    reviewBox.dataset.locked = \'\';\\n    renderReview();\\n  });\\n}\\n```\\n`box` = reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\') — fresh each submitReview ✓. Binding fresh ✓.\\n\\nOK — hmm — let me look at this from the jsdom angle: **`node.click()` on a button inside a container that ALSO... the w2 result panel — clicking #st-review-next → bubbles → ... → reviewBox — any listeners? No. → content — no. OK.\\n\\n**WAIT A MINUTE.** Let me re-examine what happens with the W2 WRONG answer more carefully — `submitReview(\'w2\', \'B\', btn)`:\\n\\n```js\\nvar correct = \'B\' === \'A\' → false;\\nvar updated = applyReviewResult(w2, false);  // ✓\\nreviewBox.querySelectorAll(\'.st-option-btn\').forEach(...add correct/wrong classes...);\\nvar banner = correct ? ... : ...;  // 答错了 banner\\n...\\nbox.innerHTML = resultHtml;   // hmm — WAIT!!!\\n```\\n\\n**`box` — WHERE IS `box` DEFINED in submitReview?!** Let me look at my submitReview code... I wrote:\\n\\n```js\\nfunction submitReview(id, letter, btn) {\\n  var w = App.store.wrongQuestions.get(id);\\n  var q = linked(w);\\n  if (!w || !q) return;\\n  var correct = ...;\\n  var updated = applyReviewResult(w, correct);\\n  ...\\n  var box = reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\');\\n  box.innerHTML = resultHtml;\\n  ...\\n  var next = box.querySelector(\'#st-review-next\');\\n  if (next) { next.addEventListener(\'click\', ...); }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nLet me verify I actually have `var box = reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\')` in the file... I wrote:\\n```js\\nvar box = reviewBox.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\');\\nbox.innerHTML = resultHtml;\\n```\\nI believe so — the static checks passed and round-1 result panels rendered ✓.\\n\\nHmm — so (B) should work... UNLESS — **`click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` in the TEST — `review` — WAIT!!! In the round-1 test code, `review` is `el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\')` — set ONCE at the beginning. After renderReview replaces reviewBox.innerHTML, the reviewBox ELEMENT ITSELF is stable (innerHTML only). `review` still points to it ✓.\\n\\nBUT — **after exitReview + enterReview... no, that\'s round 2.**\\n\\nHmm — OK — actually — WAIT. Let me recount the ROUND-1 code in the CURRENT harness3 (I edited it):\\n\\n```js\\nclick(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\');\\nvar review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\');\\nif (review.hidden) failures.push(\'wrong: 复习面板未显示\');\\nvar optA = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"A\\\"]\');\\nif (!optA) failures.push(\'wrong: 选项缺失\'); else optA.click();\\nvar result = review.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\');\\nif (!result || result.textContent.indexOf(\'答对了\') < 0) failures.push(\'wrong: 答对结果未显示\');\\nvar w1 = store.wrongQuestions.get(\'w1\');\\nif (w1.status !== \'learning\' || w1.consecutive !== 1 || w1.reviewCount !== 2) ...  // PASSED\\nif (w1.nextReview !== daysFromNow(2)) ...\\nclick(review, \'#st-review-next\');       // (A)\\nvar w2opt = review.querySelector(\'[data-opt=\\\"B\\\"]\');\\nif (!w2opt) failures.push(\'wrong: 第二题选项缺失\'); else w2opt.click();   // w2 B wrong\\nvar w2 = store.wrongQuestions.get(\'w2\');\\nif (w2.status !== \'pending\' || ...) ...   // PASSED\\nif (review.querySelector(\'#st-review-result\').textContent.indexOf(\'答错了\') < 0) ...  // PASSED\\n```\\n\\nAll round-1 assertions PASSED. So both answers applied. (A) fired (w2 panel appeared, w2opt found). Then:\\n\\n```js\\n// —— 第二轮：w1 再次答对 ——\\nclick(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\');          // ← DIRECTLY re-enter w1, NO exit first!!\\n```\\n\\n**HOLD ON!!!** Round 1 ends with w2\'s ANSWER — the result panel showing — reviewBox STILL in review mode (not exited!). The test then goes straight to round 2: `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — **but `listBox` is HIDDEN (hidden=true from enterReview) and the item elements are... STILL IN THE DOM (just hidden)!** `el.querySelector(\'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` finds the hidden item → click → enterReview(\'w1\') AGAIN → queue rebuilt → reviewIdx... → renderReview(w1) — reviewBox.innerHTML replaced with w1 panel. locked=\'1\' from w2\'s answer (round 1)!!! → **r2a click BLOCKED** ✓✓✓\\n\\n**THAT\'S THE BUG IN MY TEST — I forgot to exit review mode between round 1 and round 2!** The original v1 test had `click(review, \'[data-review-exit]\')` after next — I removed it in the rewrite! Round 1 ends with the w2 RESULT panel (not done panel — because (B) never happened in my new code — I didn\'t click next after w2\'s wrong answer in the rewritten version!!).\\n\\nLet me re-check my rewritten round-1: after w2 B wrong → assertions → then straight to round 2 comment. NO exit, NO next. So the review mode is still active with locked=\'1\'.\\n\\nFIX: after round-1 assertions, click `[data-review-exit]` to exit (the w2 result panel has it). Then round 2: click w1 item → enter → answer. Round 2 ends: answer w1 → result → next → w2 panel → answer A → then exit (result panel of w2 has exit). Round 3: click w1 → answer → archive ✓.\\n\\nLet me apply: insert `click(review, \'[data-review-exit]\');` after the round-1 w2 assertions (before round 2 comment). Also in round 2, after r2b click, the exit — result panel has [data-review-exit] ✓ click.\\n\\nAlso \'找不到元素: #st-review-next\' — round 2: `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — after r2a... r2a was BLOCKED (locked) → no result panel → no next button → \'找不到元素\' ✓ consistent. With the exit fix, r2a will apply → result → next exists ✓.\\n\\nAlso round 3 currently: after exit → `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\')` — w1 item — after exitReview, renderList re-rendered ✓.\\n\\nOne more check — round 2\'s `click(review, \'#st-review-next\')` — review variable: after round-2 enterReview, review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\') re-queried in the test ✓ (I do `review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\');` in round 2? Let me check — my round-2 code: `click(el, \'[data-review=\\\"w1\\\"]\'); review = el.querySelector(\'#st-wrong-review\'); var r2a = ...` — YES re-queried ✓.\\n\\nAnd round-2\'s next: after r2a answer → result panel with next ✓ → click → reviewIdx++ → w2 panel → r2b found → click A → w2 consecutive 1 → result → exit ✓.\\n\\nThen round 3: enter w1 → A → consecutive 3 → archived ✓ + celebration ✓. exit → list (3 items) → \'已归档\' tab → w3 + w1 = 2 ✓.\\n\\nApply the fix.\",\"content\":\"找到根因：重写时我在第一轮答完 w2 后**漏了退出复习模式**（没有点 exit），导致 `locked=\'1\'` 残留，第二轮起所有选项点击被正确拦截（产品逻辑没错，是测试流程断了）。补上退出步骤。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"summary\":\"找到根因：重写时我在第一轮答完 w2 后**漏了退出复习模式**（没有点 exit），导致 `locked=\'1\'` 残留，第二轮起所有选项点击被正确拦截（产品逻辑没错，是测试流程断了）。补上退出步骤。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":68,\"round\":68,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":null},\"round\":68,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":null}', '2026-08-03 14:55:57'),
