(2367, '36f5ade8-d69a-4f74-a7d5-ac8dc429bd14', 355, 'agent.turn.completed', 'browser', 'moonya', 'open-kimi-platform', NULL, '{\"turn_id\":\"open-kimi-platform-turn-7\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"reasoning_content\":\"The situation:\\n- web_fetch and web_crawler time out (network to proxy [runtime-host] fails)\\n- browser_automation_control start/navigate both return \\\"未知路由: POST /browser/execute\\\" - a backend routing error\\n- vls_analyze_browser says browser not started\\n\\nSo the browser automation backend seems broken. Let me try the navigate action once more with a slightly different approach. Maybe there\'s an issue with how the action is dispatched.\\n\\nLet me think about what could be the issue. The browser_automation_control tool has actions: start/navigate/click/fill/screenshot/scroll/stop. All go through POST /browser/execute. The error \\\"未知路由\\\" (unknown route) suggests the backend endpoint doesn\'t exist or is misconfigured.\\n\\nThis is likely an infrastructure issue that I can\'t directly fix. However, let me retry a couple more times to see if it\'s transient. Let me also try screenshot action to see if it works (maybe only certain actions work).\\n\\nLet me try screenshot to check browser state.\",\"content\":\"让我尝试截图操作来检查浏览器状态，并再次重试导航。\",\"content_discarded\":false,\"received_reasoning_chars\":984,\"received_content_chars\":25,\"summary\":\"让我尝试截图操作来检查浏览器状态，并再次重试导航。\",\"metadata\":{\"model\":\"deepseek-v4-flash\",\"iteration\":7,\"round\":7,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"project_group_id\":\"\",\"actor_id\":\"\",\"role_key\":\"\",\"role_label\":\"\",\"workstream\":\"\",\"owned_paths\":[],\"depends_on\":[],\"project_phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"},\"round\":7,\"phase\":\"execution\",\"project_group_id\":\"\",\"actor_id\":\"\",\"role_key\":\"\",\"role_label\":\"\",\"workstream\":\"\",\"owned_paths\":[],\"depends_on\":[],\"project_phase\":\"execution\",\"finish_reason\":\"tool_calls\"}', '2026-08-09 00:23:02'),
